   "title": "What does Bible prophecy have to say about the Iran war?",
   "url": "https://www.godreports.com/2026/10/what-does-bible-prophecy-have-to-say-about-the-iran-war/",
   "category": "missionary",
   "source": "GodReports · 宣教故事（德/国际）",
   "source_url": "https://godreports.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-12",
   "summary": "By Mark Ellis – As a 10-year-old boy, Mark Davidson’s mother gave him Hal Lindsey’s book, The Late Great Planet Earth, which eventually sold some 35 million copies, and was declared the bestselling nonfiction book of the 1970s by the New York Times. The book had a great impact on Davidson and shaped his earliest […]  The post  What does Bible prophecy have to say about the Iran war?  first appeared on  God Reports .",
   "summary_zh": "文：马克·埃利斯（Mark Ellis）——马克·戴维森（Mark Davidson）10岁时，他的母亲将哈尔·林赛（Hal Lindsey）的著作《最后的伟大地球》（The Late Great Planet Earth）送给了他。这本书最终售出约3500万册，并被《纽约时报》评为20世纪70年代最畅销的非小说类书籍。这本书对戴维森产生了深远影响，并塑造了他最早的……  文章《圣经预言对伊朗战争有何看法？》最初发表于《上帝报道》。",
   "title_zh": "圣经预言对伊朗战争有何说法？",
   "content": "By Mark Ellis – As a 10-year-old boy, Mark Davidson’s mother gave him Hal Lindsey’s book, The Late Great Planet Earth , which eventually sold some 35 million copies, and was declared the bestselling nonfiction book of the 1970s by the New York Times. The book had a great impact on Davidson and shaped his earliest views about end times Bible prophecy. Shaken by the events of 9/11, Davidson, a retired aerospace engineer, dug more deeply into end-times prophecy, seeking answers about the direction of world events.  As he dove into Scripture related to prophecy, he developed a framework that diverges from traditional teaching in several ways, and resulted in his book: Daniel Revisited : Discovering the Four Mideast Signs Leading to the Antichrist. The most relevant of his teaching to current events is his view of Iran. Based on his study of Daniel 7, Daniel 8 and Revelation 6, Davidson identified four major events, which he calls “signposts,” that he believes will unfold in the Middle East before the Tribulation. The four signposts will all be within the Islamic realm. “This interpretation involves the four beasts of Daniel 7, the ram and goat of Daniel 8, and the four horsemen of Revelation 6,” Davidson told God Reports. “They’re all talking about the same four events, just from different aspects.” He says the first signpost was fulfilled when Iraq’s government changed between 2003 and 2005, and he now sees the Iran conflict and disruption involving the Strait of Hormuz as potential indications that the second is beginning to unfold. The second signpost involves Iran (Shia) attacking its Sunni neighbors. “At some point, Iran will destroy the rest of the Arab oil infrastructure of Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, the UAE, Qatar, and Iraq,” Davidson predicts, based on his interpretation. “They’ve told the U.S. and Israel, if you attack and destroy our energy infrastructure, we’re going to do the same to all the other neighboring countries.” The attacks could be imminent, based on statements by leaders on both sides. “Iran’s threatening to do this prior to November 3 rd as an October surprise, and Trump is threatening to attack after the midterm elections. “So it could actually be quite soon where it blows up. But that’s what I see happening: the U.S. and Israel would attack Iran. Iran would fend it off like they’ve done before, destroy the rest of the Arab infrastructure, taking oil to astronomical prices.” The economic chaos and disruption could potentially threaten the US’s status as the reserve currency for the world. “Iran is going to take away the peace of mind of the entire earth,” Davidson maintains. “People will wonder how they can put food on the table.” Davidson wrote his book to warn the church because he contends the second signpost is going to be terrible. “It’s going to be awful. It’s going to change all our lives and change how we live, both in the United States as well as in much of the world. Mark Davidson “The second signpost is going to hit us in the face. I was completely aghast and flabbergasted that a U.S. president would trigger the second signpost. I was very, very surprised. “This is a whole Pandora’s box, and once the second signpost happens, that leads to the third, which leads to the fourth, which leads to the Tribulation. So, what God has done is He’s used President Trump to trigger the signpost, to trigger the coming of the Antichrist, to trigger the end of the world, and trigger Christ’s return.” If Davidson was advising President Trump, he would tell him to withdraw US forces as soon as possible. Davidson believes the rebuilding of the Jewish Temple will occur during the third signpost. He diverges from traditional teaching with his view that the coming Antichrist will be a Syrian Arab Muslim. “The ten kingdoms are not Roman kingdoms; they are Muslim kingdoms, stretching from Morocco to Pakistan,” he maintains. Some who have made comments on Davidson’s website believe the current head of Syria is one of the bes",
   "content_zh": "",
