  {
   "title": "The Biblical Doctrine of Regeneration (eBook)",
   "url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/biblical-doctrine-regeneration-ebook",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Monergism",
   "source_url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/feed",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "Edited by John Hendryx in  epub ,  .mobi  &  .pdf  formats Since faith is infinitely beyond all the power of our unregenerated human nature, it is only God who can give the spiritual ears to hear and eyes to see the beauty of Christ in the gospel. God alone disarms the hostility of the sinner turning his heart of stone to a heart of flesh (2 Cor 4:4-6). It is God, the Holy Spirit, alone who gives illumination and understanding of His word that we might believe; It is God who raises us from the d",
   "summary_zh": "由约翰·亨德里克斯（ John Hendryx ）以epub、.mobi和.pdf格式编辑，因为信心无限超越了我们未重生的人性的所有力量，只有上帝才能赐予属灵的耳朵和眼睛，在福音中看到基督的美丽。唯有神能解除罪人的敌意，把他的石心变成肉心（哥林多后书4: 4-6 ）。只有上帝，圣灵，赐予我们对他的话语的光照和理解，使我们可以相信；是上帝使我们从",
   "title_zh": "圣经重生教义（电子书）",
   "content": "Edited by John Hendryx in epub , .mobi & .pdf formats Since faith is infinitely beyond all the power of our unregenerated human nature, it is only God who can give the spiritual ears to hear and eyes to see the beauty of Christ in the gospel. God alone disarms the hostility of the sinner turning his heart of stone to a heart of flesh (2 Cor 4:4-6). It is God, the Holy Spirit, alone who gives illumination and understanding of His word that we might believe; It is God who raises us from the death of sin, who circumcises the heart; unplugs our ears; It is God alone who can give us a new sense, a spiritual capacity to behold the beauty and unsurpassed excellency of Jesus Christ. The apostle John recorded Jesus saying to Nicodemus that we naturally love darkness, hate the light and WILL NOT come into the light (John 3:19, 20). And since our hardened resistance to God is thus seated in our affections, only God, by His grace, can lovingly change, overcome and pacify our rebellious disposition. The natural man, apart from the quickening work of the Holy Spirit, will not come to Christ on his own since he is at enmity with God and cannot understand spiritual things (1 Cor 2:14). Shining a light into a blind man's eyes will not enable him to see, because eyesight first requires a set of healthy eyes.",
   "content_zh": "由John Hendryx在Epub编辑, . 惟有上帝解除了罪人将石心变成肉心的敌意(2 Cor 4:4-6). 只有真主,即圣灵,能照亮和理解我们的信仰; 真主使我们脱离罪恶之死,他割取我们的心;他揭开我们的耳朵; 只有上帝才能给我们一种新的感官,一种精神能力,来见证耶稣基督的美丽和无比杰出。 使徒约翰录制了耶稣对尼克德穆斯说,我们自然地热爱黑暗,憎恨光明并不会进入光明(John 3:19,20). 既然我们对上帝的顽强抵抗 被放在我们的慈爱中 只有上帝能以他的恩惠 慈悲地改变 克服并平息我们的叛逆 自然之人,除了\"圣灵\"的快活活外,不会独自来到基督,因为他对上帝怀有敌意并无法理解精神事物(1 Cor 2:14). 把一盏光照入一个盲人的眼中不会让他看到,因为视力首先需要一组健康的眼睛.",
   "image": "https://www.monergism.com/thethreshold/sdg/eBook_Library_HP.jpg",
   "author": "john_hendryx",
   "tags": [],
   "language": "en",
   "country": "US",
   "region": "",
   "stance": "evangelical",
   "flags": [],
   "priority": 2,
   "fetched_at": "2026-11-11T00:25:54.312499",
   "extra": {
    "feed_type": "rss20"
   },
   "id": "4e693376d5f40f2e"
  },
  {
   "title": "On Keeping the Heart (eBook)",
   "url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/keeping-heart-ebook",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Monergism",
   "source_url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/feed",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "by John Flavel Original In  ePub ,  ,mobi  &  .pdf  fomats Modernized In  ePub ,  .mobi  and  .pdf  formats Proverbs 4:23 says to keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life. Our hearts are like fortresses under attack, and we must guard them accordingly. Most people will diligently guard their fortunes and homes, which are of temporal value, but they are very careless about guarding that which is of eternal value their very souls! In this work, originally titled A Sa",
   "summary_zh": "作者： John Flavel Original在ePub中，、mobi和.pdf格式现代化在ePub中， .mobi和.pdf格式箴言4 ： 23说要全心全意地保持你的心；因为它之外是生活的问题。我们的心就像受到攻击的堡垒，我们必须相应地保护它们。大多数人会勤奋地守护自己的财富和家园，这些财富和家园具有时间价值，但他们对守护具有永恒价值的灵魂非常不小心！在这部作品中，最初的标题是A Sa",
   "title_zh": "《守护心灵》（电子书）",
   "content": "by John Flavel Original In ePub , ,mobi & .pdf fomats Modernized In ePub , .mobi and .pdf formats Proverbs 4:23 says to keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life. Our hearts are like fortresses under attack, and we must guard them accordingly. Most people will diligently guard their fortunes and homes, which are of temporal value, but they are very careless about guarding that which is of eternal value their very souls! In this work, originally titled A Saint Indeed, John Flavel (1627 1691) looks at what it means to keep the heart, how to keep the heart, and why keeping the heart is the greatest business of every person. The heart of man is his worst part before it is regenerated—and the best afterward. It is the seat of principles, and the fountain of actions. The eye of God is fixed upon it—and the eye of the Christian ought to be principally fixed upon it.",
   "content_zh": "由约翰·弗拉维尔(John Flavel)主编 在ePub中,mobi &.pdf fomats Modernized in ePub中,.mobi和.pdf格式 Proverbs 4:23表示要全心全意地保持你的心;因为其中就是生活的问题。 我们的心就像被攻击的要塞,我们必须相应地守卫它们. 大多数人会勤奋地守护着他们的财富和家园,这些财富和家园具有时间价值,但他们对于守护那些具有永恒价值的灵魂却非常不小心! 在这部原名\"A Saint Fact\"的作品中,约翰·弗拉维尔(1691年)研究了保持心意,如何保持心意,为什么保持心意是每个人最大的事业. 人心在再生之前,是他的最坏的部分,是后世最美的. 它是原则的所在地,也是行动的源泉。 真主的眼在它上面,基督教的眼在它上面。",
   "image": "https://www.monergism.com/thethreshold/sdg/eBook_Library_HP.jpg",
   "author": "john_hendryx",
   "tags": [],
   "language": "en",
   "country": "US",
   "region": "",
   "stance": "evangelical",
   "flags": [],
   "priority": 2,
   "fetched_at": "2026-11-11T00:25:54.844402",
   "extra": {
    "feed_type": "rss20"
   },
   "id": "f491a15968d21585"
  },
  {
   "title": "Systematic Theology",
   "url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/systematic-theology",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Monergism",
   "source_url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/feed",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "by Louis Berkhof In  ePub ,  .mobi  and  .pdf  formats You may also download the separate  Introductory Volume to Systematic Theology  here.  Professor Berkhof, who was the President of Calvin Seminary and professor of Systematic Theology at the same in the first half of the twentieth century, has given us an excellent compendium of Reformed theological thought in this hefty volume. The subject is treated in the classical style, moving through the Doctrines of God, Man in Relation to God, the Pe",
   "summary_zh": "作者： Louis Berkhof ePub、.mobi和.pdf格式您也可以在此处下载单独的《系统神学入门卷》。伯克霍夫教授在二十世纪上半叶担任加尔文神学院院长和系统神学教授，他在这本书中为我们提供了改革宗神学思想的出色纲要。该主题以古典风格对待，通过上帝的教义，与上帝有关的人，",
   "title_zh": "系统神学二",
   "content": "by Louis Berkhof In ePub , .mobi and .pdf formats You may also download the separate Introductory Volume to Systematic Theology here. Professor Berkhof, who was the President of Calvin Seminary and professor of Systematic Theology at the same in the first half of the twentieth century, has given us an excellent compendium of Reformed theological thought in this hefty volume. The subject is treated in the classical style, moving through the Doctrines of God, Man in Relation to God, the Person and Work of Christ, the Application of the Work of Redemption, the Church and the Means of Grace, and the Last Things. For decades, Louis Berkhof’s Systematic Theology has remained one of the most important and widely-used systematic theologies. It provides the clearest and most succinct articulation of Reformed theology. From its first publication in 1932, Berkhof’s work was revised, reprinted, and translated into Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Spanish, and Portuguese, and it had become a standard theological text by 1950. It has gained near-universal use in seminaries and Bible colleges across the world, and is widely cited and used by pastors, theologians, and students of nearly all denominational affiliations.",
   "content_zh": "由路易·伯克霍夫(Louis Berkhof)撰写 在ePub,.mobi和.pdf格式中 您也可以在此下载系统神学的单独入门卷 。 贝尔克霍夫教授曾于20世纪上半叶担任卡尔文神学院院长和系统神学教授,在本书中为我们提供了一份出色的改革神学思想简编. 主题以古典风格来对待,通过\"上帝的理论\",\"人与上帝的关系\",\"基督的人与工作\",\"救赎之作的应用\",\"教会与恩赐的手段\",\"最后的事情\"等来进行. 数十年来,路易·伯克霍夫的\"系统神学\"仍然是最重要和被广泛应用的系统神学之一. 它为改革神学提供了最清楚和最简洁的阐述。 从1932年的首次出版起,伯克霍夫的作品被修改,再版,并被翻译成了中文,日文,韩文,西班牙文和葡萄牙文,到1950年已经成为标准的神学文本. 它在世界各地的神学院和圣经学院获得了近乎普遍的使用,并被牧师、神学家和几乎所有教派派别的学生广泛引用和使用。",
   "image": "https://www.monergism.com/thethreshold/sdg/eBook_Library_HP.jpg",
