  {
   "title": "The Privileges of the True Christian",
   "url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/privileges-true-christian",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Monergism",
   "source_url": "https://www.monergism.com/blog/feed",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "J. C. Ryle \"My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me. I give eternal life to them. They will never perish, and no one will snatch them out of my hand. My Father, who has given them to me, is greater than all. No one is able to snatch them out of my Father's hand.\" (John 10:27-29) About the first part of this text, beloved, I spoke to you this morning. I told you then that this passage contains two things—first the character of true Christians, and secondly their privileges—fir",
   "summary_zh": "J. C. Ryle “我的羊听到我的声音，我知道他们，他们跟着我。我给他们永生。他们永不灭亡，谁也不能从我手里把他们夺去。我父把他们赐给我，祂比万有都大。没有人能把他们从我父的手中夺走。“ （约翰福音10:27 -29 ）亲爱的，关于这段经文的第一部分，我今天早上对你说过。我当时告诉你，这段经文包含两件事--首先是真正基督徒的品格，其次是他们的特权--",
   "title_zh": "真正基督徒的特权",
   "content": "J. C. Ryle \"My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me. I give eternal life to them. They will never perish, and no one will snatch them out of my hand. My Father, who has given them to me, is greater than all. No one is able to snatch them out of my Father's hand.\" (John 10:27-29) About the first part of this text, beloved, I spoke to you this morning. I told you then that this passage contains two things—first the character of true Christians, and secondly their privileges—first what they are to their Savior, and secondly what their Savior is to them. Let me, then, remind you what the text says of their character. \"My sheep hear My voice, and I know them, and they follow Me.\" (John 10:27) 1. God's children, His real believing people, are compared to sheep , because they are gentle, quiet, harmless and inoffensive; because they are useful and do good to all around them; because they love to be together, and dislike separation; and lastly because they are very helpless and wandering and liable to stray. 2. Jesus calls them \" My sheep ,\" as if they were His peculiar property. \"Mine,\" He would have us know, by election, \"Mine\" by purchase, and \"Mine\" by adoption. 3. Christ's sheep hear His voice, they listen humbly to His teaching, they take His word for their rule and guide. 4. Christ's sheep follow Him, they walk in the narrow path He has marked out, they do not refuse because it is sometimes steep and narrow--but wherever the line of duty lies they go forward without doubting.",
   "content_zh": "J. C. Ryle\"我的羊听到我的声音,我认识他们,他们跟着我. 我给他们永生 他们永远不会灭亡 没有人会把他们从我手中夺走 我父亲,他给我的,是比所有人更大的。 没有人能把他们从我的父亲手中夺走。” 关于这篇稿子的第一部分,亲爱的,我今天早上跟你谈过了。 我当时告诉你,这段话包含两件事——第一是真正的基督徒的个性,第二是他们的特权——第一是他们的救世主,第二是他们的救世主。 那么,让我提醒你, 文字上说他们的性格。 我的羊听见我的声音,就认识他们,他们顺从我。 真主的儿子,他的忠实的信徒,被比喻为羊,因为他们是温和的,安静的,无害的,是无罪的;因为他们是有用的,是对他们周围的人都有益的;因为他们爱在一起,不喜欢分离;最后,因为他们非常无助,而且游荡而容易迷失。 2. 耶稣称他们为\"我的羊\",好像他们是他的特有财产. \"我\",他会让我们知道,通过选举,\"我\"通过购买,\"我\"通过收养。 3. 基督的羊听到 他的声音,他们恭敬地听从他的教诲,他们以他的话为他们的统治和向导. 4. 基督的羊跟随他, 他们走在狭窄的道路 他已指出,他们不会拒绝,因为有时是陡峭和狭窄的,但无论在哪里,他们都毫不怀疑地前进。",
   "image": "https://www.monergism.com/thethreshold/sdg/eBook_Library_HP.jpg",
   "author": "john_hendryx",
