  {
   "title": "No Mask, Simply Jesus",
   "url": "https://odb.org/2026/10/31/",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "Our Daily Bread (English)",
   "source_url": "https://odb.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "In ancient Greece, actors on stage would portray the emotions of their characters by wearing masks that either expressed tragedy or comedy. Masks also allowed the same actor to play multiple roles in the same production. They weren’t permanent, nor were they representative of the real person.",
   "summary_zh": "在古希腊，舞台上的演员会戴着表达悲剧或喜剧的面具来描绘角色的情感。面具还允许同一个演员在同一个制作中扮演多个角色。它们不是永久性的，也不代表真实的人。",
   "title_zh": "没有面具，只是耶稣",
   "content": "In ancient Greece, actors on stage would portray the emotions of their characters by wearing masks that either expressed tragedy or comedy. Masks also allowed the same actor to play multiple roles in the same production. They weren’t permanent, nor were they representative of the real person.",
   "content_zh": "在古希腊，舞台上的演员会戴着表达悲剧或喜剧的面具来描绘角色的情感。面具还允许同一个演员在同一个制作中扮演多个角色。它们不是永久性的，也不代表真实的人。",
   "image": "https://odb.org/globalassets/global/logos/parent-logos/odb_parentbrand_logo_8-9-24_fullclr_icon.png?width=1200&height=680&rmode=max",
   "author": "Brent Hackett",
   "tags": [],
   "language": "en",
   "country": "US",
   "region": "",
   "stance": "evangelical",
   "flags": [],
   "priority": 2,
   "fetched_at": "2026-11-11T00:25:59.639263",
