  },
  {
   "title": "Because God!",
   "url": "https://odb.org/2026/10/28/",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "Our Daily Bread (English)",
   "source_url": "https://odb.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-08",
   "summary": "Six-year-old Tiana clasped her hands. She prayed as she scanned the crowd, glancing toward the front door of the church. Her classmates waved at guests settling in for the Father’s Day concert.",
   "summary_zh": "六岁的蒂安娜紧握双手。她一边祈祷，一边扫视人群，朝教堂前门瞥了一眼。她的同学向准备参加父亲节音乐会的客人挥手示意。",
   "title_zh": "因为上帝！",
   "content": "Our Daily Bread Devotionals",
   "content_zh": "我们的每日面包祈祷会",
   "image": "https://odb.org/globalassets/global/logos/parent-logos/odb_parentbrand_logo_8-9-24_fullclr_icon.png?width=1200&height=680&rmode=max",
   "author": "Xochitl Dixon",
   "tags": [],
   "language": "en",
   "country": "US",
   "region": "",
   "stance": "evangelical",
   "flags": [],
   "priority": 2,
   "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T23:26:31.753627",
   "extra": {
    "feed_type": "rss20"
   },
   "id": "0312c07bf502f46f"
  },
  {
   "title": "A Rich Life of Gratitude",
   "url": "https://odb.org/2026/10/27/",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "Our Daily Bread (English)",
   "source_url": "https://odb.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-07",
   "summary": "In a letter dated September 13, 1943—five months after his imprisonment for opposing the Nazi regime—Dietrich Bonhoeffer wrote his parents. He asked for books and paper. He thanked them for the ways they’d helped him, and said, “It’s a strange feeling to be so completely dependent on other people; but at least it teaches one to be grateful, and I hope I shall never forget that.",
   "summary_zh": "在他因反对纳粹政权而被监禁五个月后的1943年9月13日的一封信中，迪特里希·朋霍费尔写信给他的父母。他要书和纸。他感谢他们帮助他的方式，并说： “完全依赖他人是一种奇怪的感觉；但至少它教会了我要感恩，我希望我永远不会忘记这一点。",
   "title_zh": "丰富的感恩生活",
   "content": "In a letter dated September 13, 1943—five months after his imprisonment for opposing the Nazi regime—Dietrich Bonhoeffer wrote his parents. He asked for books and paper. He thanked them for the ways they’d helped him, and said, “It’s a strange feeling to be so completely dependent on other people; but at least it teaches one to be grateful, and I hope I shall never forget that.",
   "content_zh": "在他因反对纳粹政权而被监禁五个月后的1943年9月13日的一封信中，迪特里希·朋霍费尔写信给他的父母。他要书和纸。他感谢他们帮助他的方式，并说： “完全依赖他人是一种奇怪的感觉；但至少它教会了我要感恩，我希望我永远不会忘记这一点。",
   "image": "https://odb.org/globalassets/global/logos/parent-logos/odb_parentbrand_logo_8-9-24_fullclr_icon.png?width=1200&height=680&rmode=max",
   "author": "Monica La Rose",
   "tags": [],
   "language": "en",
   "country": "US",
   "region": "",
   "stance": "evangelical",
   "flags": [],
   "priority": 2,
   "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T23:27:59.177674",
   "extra": {
    "feed_type": "rss20"
   },
   "id": "4d97a2d1ece5bc58"
  },
  {
   "title": "God Knows Your Name",
   "url": "https://odb.org/2026/10/26/",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "Our Daily Bread (English)",
   "source_url": "https://odb.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-06",
   "summary": "One particularly catchy book promotion featured the auctioning of the chance for readers to have their name in print. Willing participants could pay to have their names used for a character in a bestselling author’s upcoming novel. The highest bidder in the auction won a chance to select a name to be used in the book.",
   "summary_zh": "一个特别引人注目的书籍促销活动是拍卖读者印刷自己的名字的机会。愿意的参与者可以付费让自己的名字用于畅销书作者即将出版的小说中的角色。拍卖中出价最高的人有机会选择要在书中使用的名称。",
   "title_zh": "神知道你的名字",
   "content": "One particularly catchy book promotion featured the auctioning of the chance for readers to have their name in print. Willing participants could pay to have their names used for a character in a bestselling author’s upcoming novel. The highest bidder in the auction won a chance to select a name to be used in the book.",
   "content_zh": "一个特别引人注目的书籍促销活动是拍卖读者印刷自己的名字的机会。愿意的参与者可以付费让自己的名字用于畅销书作者即将出版的小说中的角色。拍卖中出价最高的人有机会选择要在书中使用的名称。",
