   "summary": "The annual meetings of the Southern Baptist Convention and the Presbyterian Church in America both featured affirmations of complementarian convictions this June. The Southern Baptist Convention, which met on June 8–10 in Orlando, passed a measure to amend the constitution to provide further clarity on the ways that churches with women pastors are not in […]",
