  {
   "title": "Dogmatists Against Dogma",
   "url": "https://banneroftruth.org/us/resources/book-excerpts/2026/dogmatists-against-dogma/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Banner of Truth",
   "source_url": "https://www.banneroftruth.org/us/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "The following excerpt is from James Walker’s The Theology and Theologians of Scotland, which we have just typeset and republished in a clothbound edition. Walker is here responding to the criticism of Scottish Christianity which faults it for being too doctrinal: Then, again, I think the idea has taken possession of many in our day, that Scotch […]   The post  Dogmatists Against Dogma  appeared first on  Banner of Truth USA .",
   "summary_zh": "以下摘录来自詹姆斯·沃克（ James Walker ）的《苏格兰的神学和神学家》（ The Theology and Theologians of Scotland ） ，我们刚刚对其进行了排版，并以布面版重新出版。沃克在这里回应了对苏格兰基督教的批评，批评它过于教义化：然后，我认为这个想法在我们这个时代已经占据了许多人，苏格兰威士忌[...]后教条主义者反对教条首先出现在美国真理旗帜上。",
   "title_zh": "教条主义者反对教条",
   "content": "The following excerpt is from James Walker’s The Theology and Theologians of Scotland , which we have just typeset and republished in a clothbound edition. Walker is here responding to the criticism of Scottish Christianity which faults it for being too doctrinal: Then, again, I think the idea has taken possession of many in our day, that Scotch religion is a religion of speculative dogma, with little in it of the personal Christ. Now it seems to me there is a great deal said at present about Doctrine or Dogma which means nothing. How can you act in regard to or feel about a thing, save as you have some conception and some opinion concerning it? You must have some opinion about the person of Christ, if He is to be an element in your practical life. How can He act on you otherwise? And, therefore, as you are Trinitarian, or Arian, or Unitarian, or Humanitarian, or something else, so will be the effect on you. And, in fact, the man who abuses dogmas is as much a dealer in dogmas as his neighbours. What is it but a dogma—generally asserted, indeed, with a fierce and contemptuous fanaticism, and carried out with a remorseless logic—that there should be no dogmas? Like scepticism, this sort of thing kills itself. Say what men will, all action, all organization, all religious or irreligious fellowship, is based upon a Credo. In regard to many who bring the accusation most readily about Scottish doctrinalism, I assert that there are none more doctrinal than themselves. The Broad Churchman maintains the doctrine of the Divine Fatherhood; puts that doctrine into definite conception; argues on the basis of that doctrine to immense conclusions, which make illusive a large amount of the deepest and most powerful experiences of Christian history. The Unitarian maintains the doctrine of the Divine Unity, and evolves therefrom proposition after proposition, overthrowing, as he thinks, all the life-giving Christian beliefs. The real truth is that orthodoxy is chary of the speculative. Mystery is one of its fundamental ideas. The Theosophic 1 belongs far more to heterodox Alexandrianism than orthodox Augustinianism. I do not think that it can be affirmed of Calvin, that he was as supreme in the metaphysical or speculative as in all else. Certainly our Scottish theology is not in any proper sense a metaphysical system, though there has been often a cloud or a halo of metaphysics about it, but the product in the main of an honest study of the Bible and a practical religious experience. The doctrines which have been prominently taught among us, such as the atonement of Christ, justification, the new birth, the indwelling of the Holy Ghost, are not in any sense speculative human reasonings, but transcendent facts,—mysteries which, according to all experience, tell with prodigious power on the human soul, and take hold of the deepest convictions of the least philosophical and cultured. Buy the Book: The Theology and Theologians of Scotland In the Seventeenth and Eighteenth Centuries by Walker, James price $ 28.00 Original price was: $28.00. $ 25.20 Current price is: $25.20. Learn More Add to Cart Description Endorsements ‘A masterly work . . . in its own department, a classic.’ — JOHN MACLEOD ‘The standard work on the subject.’ — NICK NEEDHAM Book Description James Walker (1821–1891) belongs to that rare class of individuals who have been able to master the theological literature of a nation. This valuable book contains the fruit […] Featured Picture (visible when article shared online): Alexander Nasmyth, 1758–1840, View of the City of Edinburgh, ca. 1822, Oil on canvas, Yale Center for British Art, Paul Mellon Collection, B1974.3.21. 1    Presumably here the idea intended is that the knowledge of God can be achieved through direct intuition. The post Dogmatists Against Dogma appeared first on Banner of Truth USA .",
   "content_zh": "以下摘录出自詹姆斯·沃克的\"苏格兰神学与神学\",我们刚刚对它进行打字并重新以布满的版本出版. 沃克在此回应苏格兰基督教的批评, 然后,我再说一遍,我认为这个想法在我们这个时代已经占有了许多人, 苏格兰宗教是一种投机教条的宗教, 很少包含个人的基督。 现在,在我看来,目前关于理论或道格玛的说法很多,这毫无意义。 除了你对某件事有某种概念和看法之外,你怎么能对某件事采取行动或感觉呢? 如果上帝要成为你实际生活中的一个要素,你一定对基督的人有些看法. 怎么会 他对你另当别论? 因此,既然你是三硝基亚人,或亚利安人,或统一人,或人道,或别的东西,那么,对你们的影响也会是这样。 事实上 虐待教条的人 和邻居一样是教条商人 除了一个教条外,什么是不应该有教条的? 教条一般是用一种激烈而可鄙的狂热主义来断言的,并且以毫无悔恨的逻辑来进行。 类似怀疑,这种东西会自杀。 说男人的意志,所有的行动,所有组织,所有宗教或非宗教的研究金,都是建立在克里多之上的. 对于许多最容易指控苏格兰教条主义的人,我断言,没有什么比他们自己更多的教条了。 Broad Churchman坚持了神之父的教义;将该教义置于明确的概念之中;基于该教义而论证了巨大的结论,这些结论使基督教历史上大量最深刻和最强大的经验变得虚幻。 统一主义者坚持\"神通统一\"的学说,并从中演化出在命题后的建议,推翻了他所想的,所有赋予生命的基督教信仰. 真正的事实是,正统性是投机性的魅力。 神秘主义是其基本思想之一. 相较于正统的奥古斯丁主义,\"神话一\"更属于异体的亚历山大主义. 我并不认为卡尔文能被证实 他在物理或推测方面 和所有其他方面一样至高无上 当然,我们的苏格兰神学在任何适当的意义上都不是一个元物理系统,尽管关于它经常有云或光环的元物理,但主要产物是对\"圣经\"进行诚实研究并实践宗教经验. 在我们中间受到突出教导的理论,如赎罪、辩护、新诞生、使圣灵安息等,从任何意义上讲,都不是推测人类的推理,而是超越的事实,根据所有的经验,这些神话以对人类灵魂的超乎寻常的力量加以说明,并信奉哲学和文化最低的信念。 沃克17和18世纪的苏格兰神学和神学家,詹姆斯价格28.00美元 原价:28.00美元 现价:25.20美元 \" 在自己的部门里学习更多的加进纸板描述认可 \" 。 – NICK NESTHAM Book Direct James Walker(1821–1891)属于能够掌握一个国家神学文献的这一稀有阶层。 这本珍贵的书里有水果... Featured Picture(在线分享文章时可见):Alexander Nasmyth, 1758–1840, 《爱丁堡市的景色》, 约1822年, 《油画》, 耶鲁英国艺术中心, Paul Mellon Collection, B1974.3.21。 1 这里设想的意向是,对上帝的了解可以通过直接直觉实现。 抗道格玛(Dogmatists against Dogma)后,",
