  {
   "title": "In the Christian Life, There is No One ‘Master Key’",
   "url": "https://banneroftruth.org/us/resources/articles/2026/in-the-christian-life-there-is-no-one-master-key/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Banner of Truth",
   "source_url": "https://www.banneroftruth.org/us/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-05",
   "summary": "The first of six posts containing the substance of teaching given by Albert N. Martin at the 1984 Banner Youth Conference, presenting a basic biblical theology of the Christian life. A question of major importance is ‘How am I to live as a Christian’? It is one thing to be certain on biblical grounds that […]   The post  In the Christian Life, There is No One ‘Master Key’  appeared first on  Banner of Truth USA .",
   "summary_zh": "六个帖子中的第一个帖子包含了阿尔伯特· N ·马丁（ Albert N. Martin ）在1984年旗帜青年大会（ Banner Youth Conference ）上给出的教学内容，展示了基督教生活的基本圣经神学。一个非常重要的问题是“我如何作为基督徒生活” ？从圣经的角度来看，可以肯定的一件事是[…]在基督徒的生活中，没有一个“万能钥匙”首先出现在美国真理旗帜上。",
   "title_zh": "在基督徒的生活中，没有“万能钥匙”",
   "content": "The first of six posts containing the substance of teaching given by Albert N. Martin at the 1984 Banner Youth Conference, presenting a basic biblical theology of the Christian life. A question of major importance is ‘How am I to live as a Christian’? It is one thing to be certain on biblical grounds that I have life from Christ, now I must be clear as to how I am to live the life of Christ. My purpose in setting before you some of the major principles of living the Christian life is three-fold: —I wish to sketch in a biblical theology of the Christian life. My purpose is unashamedly one of indoctrination. I wish by God’s help, by Spirit and word, to indoctrinate you in a basic biblical theology of the Christian life. —I wish to inoculate you and to immunize you against the major false views of the Christian life. Some of us desperately wish we had received such an inoculation early in our Christian experience. We spent many years chasing rabbits that we could never catch. We went after experiences and states of mind and heart in the hope that somehow in so doing we would find what it really meant to live as a Christian. —I wish to purge you of any existing misconceptions which you may presently have. It may not be pleasant but it is in your own best interests. We now examine these major principles of the Christian life. Principle 1: There is No One ‘Master Key’ to Living the Christian Life The kind of teaching I am purposing to focus upon in this principle goes something like this: There is a Christian who for many years has found himself in the doldrums. He has had his sails hoisted but he goes nowhere. It seems that he knows little of the wind of the Spirit filling his sails and carrying him anywhere. Or, to change the analogy, he may have his sails hoisted but they seem for ever to be full of holes, and while all around him have hoisted sails and appear to be making progress he seems to be going nowhere. And then one day at a conference or while reading a book or in his own devotions he comes across a passage of Scripture, say John chapter 15, and there he reads in the words of our Lord Jesus that beautiful analogy of the Christian’s relationship to Christ as the relationship of a branch to a vine. This so ignites his own spiritual life that he is almost overnight lifted to an entirely new plateau of spiritual vitality. Either the holes in his sails get mended or it is as though a mighty zephyr from God himself fills his sails, causing them to billow out to the full. He makes more substantial progress in the Christian life in six months than he has made in the previous six years. This man says that the master key to the Christian life is understanding John 15 and if others will only come to understand the concept of Christ’s relationship to his people as the branch and the vine are related they too will come to an entirely new plateau of spiritual vitality and reality in their Christian walk. Another example could be someone who has been struggling with a certain besetting sin which leaves him continually bowed down and crippled with guilt. Here is a young Christian struggling with a certain area of besetting sin, unknown to others, and he is constantly bogged down. His wheels are up to the hub-caps in mud, and no matter how much he changes the gears and pushes down on the accelerator he is spinning his wheels and all he is doing is using up petrol and making a mess. He is in that position for weeks and months perhaps, and then one day at a conference or reading a book or in his own devotions he comes to Romans, chapter 6, and he reads the glorious truth that in union with Jesus Christ all that he was as old man has been put to death, and in union with Jesus Christ the totality of the old life has been buried in Christ’s tomb and he is now a new man in Jesus Christ and he sees that he is called upon to reckon it so, and in the light of that, present himself as alive from the dead. He reads the statement, ‘Sin shall not exe",
   "content_zh": "阿尔伯特·N·马丁在1984年班纳青年大会上发表的六篇包含教学内容的文章中的一篇文章,介绍了基督教生活的基本圣经神学. 一个非常重要的问题是:我如何作为一个基督徒活下来? 从圣经上确定我的生命来自基督是一回事,现在我必须明白我如何活基督的生命.\n在你们面前,我提出一些关于基督教生活的主要原则,目的有三个方面:——我想在圣经中描绘基督教生活的神学. 我的目的就是毫不羞愧地教化别人 我希望通过上帝的帮助,通过精神和文字,将你灌输到基督教生活的基本圣经神学中去.\n我希望为你们接种疫苗,并为你们接种疫苗,反对基督教生活中的重大错误观点。 我们当中有些人非常希望我们早期在基督教经验中得到这样的接种。 我们花了很多年 追赶我们永远抓不到的兔子\n我们追寻经验 和精神状态和心境, 希望能找到作为基督徒生活的真正意义。 我希望清除你目前可能存在的任何误解。 这也许不愉快,但符合你的最佳利益。 我们现在审查基督教生活的这些主要原则。\n然后有一天,在会议中,或者在读到一本书时,或者在自己的奉献中,他穿过了圣经的一行,如约翰·第15章,他用我们的主耶稣的话来读到,把基督教与基督的关系比作树枝与藤条的关系。\n这如此点燃了他自己的精神生活,以至于几乎一夜之间被抬到一个全新的精神活力高地. 要么他的帆上有洞被修补好 要么就好像上帝亲自放出一个强大的快活器 来灌入他的帆上 让他们满地找牙 他在6个月里在基督教生活中取得了比前6年更大的实质性进步.\n这个人说,基督教生活的主要关键在于理解约翰·15,如果其他人只了解基督与其人民的关系概念,因为树枝和藤蔓是相连的,他们也会在基督教行走中来到一个精神活力和现实的全新的高地。\n另一个例子是,有人一直在为某种困扰他的罪行而挣扎,使他不断屈从并因罪恶而致残。 这里有一个年轻的基督教徒在挣扎着 某些困扰的罪恶领域, 其他人不知道, 他经常陷入困境。\n他的车轮在泥地上被吊起,无论他如何改变齿轮并推倒了加速器,他正在旋转他的车轮,他所做的就是用上汽油并制造一团糟。\n赫里斯特和他看到,他被召唤去 如此估计, 并据此, 现身 活着 从死亡。 他读了这段话,",
