  {
   "title": "The Beauty of the Law",
   "url": "https://www.challies.com/sponsored/the-beauty-of-the-law/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Tim Challies",
   "source_url": "https://www.challies.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-08",
   "summary": "Encounter the living Jesus in all of Scripture. The Jesus Bible lifts Jesus up as the lead story of the Bible and encourages you to faithfully follow him as you participate in his story. See Also New and Notable Christians Books for December Free Stuff Fridays (Zondervan Reflective) Free Stuff Fridays (Zondervan Reflective)",
   "summary_zh": "在全部圣经中遇到活着的耶稣。耶稣圣经将耶稣提升为圣经的主要故事，并鼓励你在参与他的故事时忠实地跟随他。另请参阅新的和著名的基督徒书籍十二月免费的东西周五（ Zondervan Reflective ）免费的东西周五（ Zondervan Reflective ）",
   "title_zh": "法律的美丽",
   "content": "This week, the blog is sponsored by Zondervan . This article is taken from The Jesus Bible , from Passion Publishing and Zondervan. The Lord called Joshua to be strong and courageous as Joshua replaced Moses as Israel’s leader and led the people into the promised land. This calling was based on his obedience and submission to the Word of God. As the Creator, God knows how life is meant to be lived and the way for people to experience life to the full ( Jn 10:10). The gift of the law was a gracious act of God to instruct his people in his ways. It was never intended to be a moralistic plan to earn God’s favor. Rather, the law was given to those who had already experienced God’s redeeming grace. In the law, God provided instructions for how his children can love him and other people. This law is not a collection of arbitrary dictates from a malevolent deity, but instead it is the wisdom of God distilled in human language. It is a path to joy and life — the way people were meant to live. The Bible continually portrays the law of God in this fashion. For example, in the longest psalm in the Bible, Psalm 119, the author says that he loves, treasures, delights in and longs for the law. It is a source of hope, peace, joy and direction. In Psalm 19, the psalmist says the law refreshes the soul, makes wise the simple, gives joy to the heart and gives light to the eyes (Ps 19:7 – 8). The law is a beautiful gift from a gracious God. Jesus testified to the lasting value of the law when he said that he did not come to abolish the law (Mt 5:17). Instead, Jesus amplified the law, explaining the transformation that should result as a proper response to his work. In his masterful Sermon on the Mount in Matthew 5 through 7, Jesus called people to a far greater standard of obedience than mere conformity to external regulations. Instead of simply condemning murder, Jesus unmasked the anger that fueled this act. Adultery is not the prime culprit, but lust rooted in the human heart is the real problem. Jesus methodically outlined the heart-level change that the law relied upon. Rather than rendering the law obsolete, Jesus showed that the law continued to provide an authoritative standard and guidance for God’s people. Now, because of the finished work of Christ, believers have hope that the price for their disobedience of the law has been paid and that they have God’s Spirit dwelling within them, providing them the power to live the life God intends. See Also New and Notable Christians Books for December Free Stuff Fridays (Zondervan Reflective) Free Stuff Fridays (Zondervan Reflective)",
   "content_zh": "博客由Zondervan赞助, 这篇文章取自\"耶稣圣经\",\"激情出版\"和\"赞德凡\". 耶和华召约书亚为强而勇敢,因为约书亚取代了摩西成为以色列领导人并带领人民进入所应许之地. 这个召唤是基于他的服从和顺从上帝之道.\n\n作为造物主,上帝知道生命的本意,知道人们如何体验到生命的完全(Jn 10:10). 法律的天赋是上帝的恩惠行为,以指示他的人民如何行事. 这从来就没有打算成为赢得上帝恩惠的道德计划。 相反,法律是给予那些已经经历过上帝赎回恩惠的人的。\n\n在法律中,上帝为他的孩子如何能爱他和其他人提供了指示. 这部法则并不是从邪恶的神灵中任意地指令的集合,而是用人类语言来提炼出上帝的智慧. 这是通往快乐和生活的道路——人们本该生活的方式。 圣经以这种方式不断地描绘出上帝的法则.\n\n耶稣作证了法律的持久价值,他说他不是来废除法律的(Mt 5:17). 相反地,耶稣放大了律法,解释了应该因适当回应他的工作而导致的转变. 在他精通马太福音5号到7号的\"山上赛蒙\"中,耶稣把人们称为服从的标准远远高于单纯遵守外规.\n\n耶稣不是简单地谴责谋杀,而是揭发了激起这一行为的愤怒. 通奸不是罪魁祸首,但植根于人心的欲望才是真正的问题. 耶稣有条不紊地概述了法律所依赖的心脏层面的变化. 耶稣没有使法律过时,而是表明法律继续为上帝的人民提供权威的标准和指导.\n\n现在,由于基督的完成,信徒们希望他们违抗法律的代价已经付出,他们心中有上帝的精神,给他们以神想要的生活的力量。 另见12月自由聚会(Zondervan反省会)12月自由聚会(Zondervan反省会)自由聚会(Zondervan反省会)的基督教新书。",
   "image": "https://www.challies.com/media/2026/11/Jesus-Bible_tan_1920x1080.jpg",
   "author": "Tim Challies",
   "tags": [
    "Sponsored"
   ],
   "language": "en",
   "country": "CA",
   "region": "",
   "stance": "evangelical",
   "flags": [],
   "priority": 2,
   "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T23:26:39.597768",
   "extra": {
    "feed_type": "rss20"
   },
   "id": "148bce066112e225"
  },
  {
   "title": "Tips for Resolving Conflict in Marriage",
   "url": "https://www.challies.com/articles/tips-for-resolving-conflict-in-marriage/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Tim Challies",
   "source_url": "https://www.challies.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-08",
   "summary": "Conflict in marriage is inevitable, but resolving it well is a skill. Here are 6 practical tips that range from examining your own sin first to a 10 p.m. rule. See Also Danger Signs of an Unhealthy Dating Relationship The Beginner’s Guide to Conflict Resolution Free Stuff Fridays",
   "summary_zh": "婚姻中的冲突是不可避免的，但妥善解决冲突是一项技能。这里有6个实用技巧，从先检查你自己的罪到晚上10点的规则。另请参阅不健康约会关系的危险迹象周五解决冲突的初学者指南免费内容",
   "title_zh": "解决婚姻冲突的技巧",
   "content": "It is inevitable that lives lived in deep intimacy will generate conflict. We wish this weren’t so, but sadly, it is. Therefore, wise couples learn to anticipate conflict and learn to resolve it well. I was recently asked to provide some thoughts on conflict resolution, and thought I’d share what I came up with. Yet as I have sat with couples and tried to help them work through various issues, it has shocked me to find how many have never learned to settle conflict well. Many set habits and patterns in their early years that become hard to break or overcome. I have met with couples who have only ever tried to resolve conflict by raising their voices, and with others who have only ever tried to resolve it by going silent. I have met with some who have only ever relied on text messaging instead of speaking face to face, and with others who have long since given up and don’t even bother trying anymore. Much of this stems from their first years and their failure to get well grounded in conflict resolution. To that end, here are a few suggestions on resolving conflict well. First, borrowing from Robert Murray M’Cheyne, follow this pattern: For every one look at your spouse’s sin, take ten at your own. It’s easy enough to become an expert in the way your spouse sins against you, but it’s far more important to become an expert in the ways you sin against your spouse. It concerns me when I see someone who seems adamantly committed to his spouse’s holiness but seemingly not very interested in his own. Your first calling before the Lord is to deal with your own sin so you can put it to death and come alive to righteousness. Second, invite your spouse to identify your sin. Because of the sheer quantity of the time and intimacy you share, you will inevitably sin against your spouse more than you will sin against anyone else. Not only that, but married life lets your spouse see the kinds of sins that no one else will. Only he or she sees how you sin in the bedroom, for example, or when you’re running late and nobody else is around. What’s more, your spouse sees deeper into your soul than anyone else and, therefore, knows more about you. In a healthy marriage, if you are truly committed to holiness, it only makes sense that you will ask your spouse to speak into your life. It is wise to provide a safe setting to do this where you won’t be a baby or a bully, and won’t sulk or lash out. Set aside some time, tell your spouse that you’d like to hear what sins you are committing, then listen patiently and calmly, without showing anger or being defensive. Having done that, go away, think about it, pray about it, and don’t respond until a day later. This could be a great means of grace in your life. Third, identify times when you won’t try to resolve conflict. Aileen and I, for example, have a long-established 10 o’clock rule, which means we won’t try to fix anything after 10 p.m. We are well aware that Ephesians 4:26 says, “Do not let the sun go down on your anger,” but we have also learned that some issues simply cannot be neatly resolved by bedtime. (Married folk will know that some of the most common conflicts tend to happen between the time you get into bed together and the time you actually fall asleep.) The later the day gets, the more we tend to operate out of emotion rather than reason. And some things seem way worse in the evening when we’re tired than in the morning when we’re fresh. So if we haven’t worked it out by 10, we will call a halt, kiss one another, pray with one another, say something like “I love you and we are going to be all right,” and then go to sleep. Then we can try to work it out at a better time, when we are in a better frame of mind. And honestly, in the light of day, we often realize the situation wasn’t nearly as dire as we thought and that it can be covered by love (1 Peter 4:8). Fourth, invite others in when necessary. Sometimes the most helpful thing you can do in a time of conflict is invite some friends or so",
   "content_zh": "生活在深深的亲密中的生活必然会引发冲突。 但可悲的是, 因此,明智的夫妇学会预测冲突并学会妥善解决冲突。 最近有人要求我提出一些解决冲突的想法,\n\n然而,当我与夫妇们坐在一起,努力帮助他们解决各种问题时,我发现有多少人从未学会妥善解决冲突,这让我感到震惊。 许多人在早年就设定了难以打破或克服的习惯和模式.\n\n我见过夫妇们,他们只试图通过提高声音来解决冲突,而其他人则只试图通过沉默来解决冲突。 我会见了一些只依靠短信而不是面对面发言的人,\n\n其主要原因是他们最初的岁月和未能在解决冲突中扎根。 为此,我们提出一些关于妥善解决冲突的建议。 首先,向罗伯特·默里·姆谢恩借款,遵循这一模式: 每看一看配偶的罪孽,就自己拿十。\n\n成为你配偶对你的罪过的专家是很容易的, 当我看到有人 似乎坚定致力于他的配偶的圣洁,\n\n你第一次在主面前召唤是 处理你自己的罪过 这样你就可以把它死 并活到正义。 其次,请您的配偶 识别你的罪恶。 由于你所分享的时间和亲密关系,你不可避免地会对你的配偶犯下比对其他人犯下更严重的罪行。\n\n不仅如此 婚姻生活让你的配偶看到 别人不会犯的罪 只有他或她看到你在卧室的罪过, 更何况,你的配偶比任何人都更深刻地看待你的灵魂,从而更了解你。\n\n在一个健康的婚姻中,如果你真正致力于圣洁,那么你要求你的配偶在你的生活中说话就只有道理了. 最好提供安全的环境,\n\n也不要发怒或防卫。 并且直到一天后才回应。 这可能是你生命中伟大的恩典手段. 第三,确定你何时不会试图解决冲突。\n\n例如艾琳和我早就有十点的规则, 我们清楚地知道,以弗所4:26说,“不要让太阳落在你的愤怒上,”但我们也了解到,有些问题根本不能通过睡觉来彻底解决。\n\n(结婚后人们会知道,一些最常见的冲突往往发生在你们上床睡觉的时间与实际入睡的时间之间. 一天越晚,我们就越倾向于出于情感而不是理性而行动. 有些事情在晚上比早上更糟糕,\n\n因此,如果我们还没有在10点之前解决,我们将叫停,互相亲吻,相互祈祷,说出类似“我爱你,我们会没事的”的话,然后睡觉。 然后,我们可以尝试在更好的时间,当我们处于一个更好的思维框架时,解决它。\n\n老实说,在白天,我们常常意识到,情况没有我们想象的那么糟糕,而且可以被爱所覆盖(1:彼得:8). 第四,在必要时邀请其他人参加。 有时候,在冲突时期,你能做的最有帮助的事 就是邀请一些朋友",
   "image": "https://www.challies.com/media/2026/11/Warm-Bedside-Clock-and-Book.png",
