  {
   "title": "Works & Wonders (November 1)",
   "url": "https://www.challies.com/articles/works-wonders-november-1/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Tim Challies",
   "source_url": "https://www.challies.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-07",
   "summary": "This week’s Works & Wonders: God’s power paired with his goodness, Wikipedia’s most-read page, weather photos, Anchor Hymns, a one-trick app, and men who sing. See Also Works & Wonders: October 25 Works & Wonders (Oct 11) Works & Wonders (August 2)",
   "summary_zh": "本周的作品与奇迹：上帝的力量与他的善良、维基百科阅读量最大的页面、天气照片、锚定赞美诗、单一技巧应用程序和唱歌的人相结合。另请参阅作品与奇观： 10月25日作品与奇观（ 10月11日）作品与奇观（ 8月2日）",
   "title_zh": "作品与奇观（ 11月1日）",
   "content": "In my weekly Works & Wonders column, I combine a brief devotional with other interesting and uplifting bits and pieces I gleaned throughout the week. I hope you enjoy this week’s collection! It includes: When God Acts in Power Wikipop Weather Photographer of the Year Bring on the Dawn Big Words Men Sing 1. When God Acts in Power No element of God’s character can be separated from any other. You or I may use the power available to us recklessly, imperfectly, or sinfully—we may act forcefully yet unwisely, or authoritatively yet with evil motives and immoral outcomes. We may act impulsively, on the basis of false information, or in ways that foster prejudice or injustice. In this way, power can be used to bring about great good or great harm. But God never acts in such a way that he diminishes any part of his character. Hence, when God acts in power, he invariably exercises that power in ways that are wise, holy, just, good, and true. I think Jen Wilkin says this well: “The truth of God’s limitless power would be absolutely terrifying were it not paired with the truth of His limitless goodness.” God’s power separated from his other attributes would mean there is nothing that would withhold or restrain him. Yet God’s power paired with his other attributes is tremendously comforting, for we know he will use his power only in ways that are ultimately for our good and his glory. 2. Wikipop Wikipop is a microsite that offers the answer to just one question: What Wikipedia page was everyone looking at yesterday? You probably won’t be shocked to know that on Saturday, when I finalized this article, it told me that everyone had been looking for Patrick Stewart, who died a few days prior. (Note: I add this site with a bit of trepidation because I can’t predict what article will be featured on the day you click the link, so hopefully it’s nothing bad!) 3. Weather Photographer of the Year I know I keep sharing photography contests, but as I said last week, this is the time of year when many of them announce the winners. But this one is different from others I have shared since it features weather. In the Weather Photographer of the Year shortlist, you’ll find exactly what you’d expect—a stunning collection of photos of the weather. 4. Bring on the Dawn I know many people who have appreciated Douglas McKelvey’s Every Moment Holy books, which offer liturgies and prayers for all of life’s moments. Anchor Hymns recently collaborated with McKelvey on an album titled Bring on the Dawn that was inspired by his books. I’m pretty sure that if you appreciate the books, you’ll also like the music. 5. Big Words Sometimes the best apps are the simplest—the ones that do just one thing, but do it well. That’s the case with Big Words . What does it do? It lets you use your phone (or iPad or other screen) to display big words. “Make a full-screen sign, timer or message from a link. Hold up your phone at arrivals, put a countdown on the TV, or show the Wi-Fi password at the front desk. No account, no app, nothing stored on a server. The link is the whole display, so you can share it or bookmark it.” There is nothing to download, so you can just go ahead and bookmark it to use when the need arises. 6. Men Sing I love this delightfully countercultural “Men Sing” trend that’s happening among Dutch Reformed churches, and would love to see it spread. What is it? It’s just men getting together to sing hymns. I had hoped to attend the recent one in Hamilton, but was on the road at the time. Hopefully I can make it to the next one. You can find videos from churches in Hamilton , Grand Rapids , and Chilliwack . I assume it’s happening in other places where there are lots of Dutch Reformed churches. Well done, Dutch guys! See Also Works & Wonders: October 25 Works & Wonders (Oct 11) Works & Wonders (August 2)",
   "content_zh": "在每周的Works & Wonders专栏中,我把简短的奉献与我整个星期所收集的其他有趣而令人振奋的作品结合起来。 希望你们能欣赏这周的作品! 它包括: 当上帝在权力中的行为 维基百科中的相关条目: 天气摄影师 这一年带来黎明的大字眼 男人会唱歌 1 当上帝在权力中行事时,神性的任何要素都不能与任何其他要素相分离。\n你或我可能会莽撞地、不完美地、或罪恶地使用我们所拥有的权力——我们可能会以邪恶的动机和不道德的结果,采取强而不明智或权威的行动。 我们可能根据虚假信息或以助长偏见或不公正的方式采取冲动行动。 这样,权力可以用来带来巨大的好坏.\n但上帝从不以这样的方式行事,以致于削弱他性格的任何部分. 因此,当上帝行使权力时,他总是以明智、神圣、公正、善良和真实的方式行使这种权力。\n我认为Jen Wilkin说得好 : “ 如果上帝无限力量的真理不与他无限善良的真理相配的话,那将是绝对可怕的。 ” 神的力量与他的其他属性相分离,将意味着没有任何东西可以扣留或约束他.\n然而,上帝的力量与他的其他属性相配,是极为安慰的,因为我们知道,他只会以最终有利于我们及其光荣的方式使用他的力量。 2. Wikipop Wikipop是一个微站点,只回答一个问题:昨天大家看的维基百科页面是什么?\n你可能不会惊讶地知道, 星期六我写完这篇文章时, (注:我加上这个网站有点惊慌, 因为我无法预测您点击链接当天会刊登什么文章, 3个\n天气摄影师,我知道我一直 分享摄影比赛, 但正如我上周所说, 但这个与我分享的其他不同,因为它的特点是天气。 在年度天气摄影短名单中, 你会找到你所期望的,  4.四.\n我认识很多人欣赏道格拉斯·麦克凯维的\"每一分一秒\"的书, Anchor Hymns最近与McKelvey合作, 我敢肯定,如果你欣赏这些书,你也会喜欢音乐。 5 (韩语).\n大词 有时最好的应用最简单, 大字报就是这样。 这有什么用? 它让你使用手机(或iPad或其他屏幕)来显示大字. “从链接中制作全屏标志、定时器或信息。 电话在到达时暂停,在电视上倒计时,或在前台显示无线密码.\n没有账户 没有应用 没有存储在服务器上 链接是整个显示,所以你可以分享它或者书签它。” 没有什么可以下载的,所以你可以继续去书签,以便在需要的时候使用. 六. 男子歌唱我爱这种令人愉快的反文化\"男子歌\"趋势, 这是什么?\n只是男人聚在一起唱颂歌。 我本来希望参加最近在汉密尔顿的比赛 但当时还在路上 希望我能赶到下一个 在汉密尔顿、大拉皮兹和奇利瓦克的教堂, 我想这发生在其他地方, 干得好,荷兰人!\n也参见\"作品与神奇\":10月25日 \"作品与奇幻\" (Oct 11) \"作品与奇幻\" (August 2)",
   "image": "https://www.challies.com/media/2026/10/WW-Banner-Templates-1.png",
   "author": "Tim Challies",
