  {
   "title": "A La Carte (October 29)",
   "url": "https://www.challies.com/a-la-carte/a-la-carte-october-29-2026/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Tim Challies",
   "source_url": "https://www.challies.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-04",
   "summary": "8 Ways to help your kids love the church / I hate your Halloween decorations / How mental illness became an identity / It can happen here, too / How the mainstream recruits for the manosphere / Why paper books endure / Kindle deals, and more See Also Weekend A La Carte (December 27) A La Carte (October 2) Kindle Deals for Christian Readers",
   "summary_zh": "帮助孩子爱上教堂的8种方法/我讨厌你的万圣节装饰品/精神疾病如何成为一种身份/也可能在这里发生/庄园的主流新兵如何忍受/Kindle优惠等另请参阅周末单点（ 12月27日）单点（ 10月2日）基督教读者的Kindle优惠",
   "title_zh": "点菜（ 10月29日）",
   "content": "Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ. Sales & Deals Today’s Kindle deals include books about the Old Testament, Proverbs, faithful presence, the life and influence of Tim Keller, and a whole lot more. Westminster Books is continuing their Reformation sale by offering discounts on ESV Bibles as well as the tremendous new 500th anniversary edition of Tyndale’s New Testament. Recommended Reading How the Mainstream Recruits for the Manosphere. Aaron Renn explains how “asymmetric blame, hectoring lectures, and selectively revived norms are driving young men to the influencers the mainstream condemns.” How Mental Illness Became an Identity. Myles Werntz has an interesting review of a new book by Fredrik deBoer that explains how mental illness became an identity. “Mental illness in the 21st century is an expanding category—and one increasingly dominated by its most functional and therefore visible members. That displacement—in our collective imagination and public discourse—of the profoundly mentally ill by my college students didn’t happen all at once. And how did it happen? Was it because of the closure of traditional mental hospitals, like those of One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest ? Was it because of the internet-driven phenomenon of self-diagnosis by very functional influencers? The marginalization of psychiatry as a profession? Or denial, romanticization, and politics?” It Can Happen Here, Too. “As numerous countries in Europe experience riots, many in America are asking, ‘What on earth is happening on the continent that was, in many ways, the cradle of Western civilization?’ As historic buildings, places of worship, and commercial properties combust before our eyes on the nightly news, how are we to make sense of this?” Carl Trueman warns that what’s happening in Europe could also happen in the United States. 8 Ways to Help Your Kids Love the Church. Shiphrah Lakka offers a series of ways to help your kids learn to love the church. “While discipleship at home is extremely important and something every Christian parent should pursue, it can never replace the church. Reading Scripture together, praying as a family, and teaching our children about God within our homes are vital practices. Yet God’s design for believers extends beyond the walls of our homes. He calls us to belong to a community of believers who worship, serve, and do life together.” I Hate Your Halloween Decorations. Marc Sims writes about the reality of Halloween today. “The next time I am out, we will really slow down to take in the diorama you set up of black hooded figures encircling a pentagram-alter with a fake infant set in the middle of it, that way he can become familiar with Satanic rituals and child sacrifice. I mean, where else is he going to get this important cultural experience? Apparently, you are under the impression that becoming desensitized to violence and death is an important step for our whole neighborhood to take in—to celebrate, even. Here, frumpy old Marc ( boooo! ) was worried about why our culture seems ever more eager to relish death and the demonic—but you have shown me that this is really just fun! Save a fake a corpse for me!” Why Paper Books Endure. Daniel Darling explains his ongoing love for paper books (even while he’s not entirely opposed to electronic ones). “When I began my writing career in the early 2,000s, every single writing conference I attended featured speakers who issued grave warnings. E-books would eventually take over. Paper books would be a thing of the past. Libraries are nice relics of another era. Except that didn’t happen.” Something Worth Doing These words by Maltbie Davenport Babcock have often been a challenge to me, and I wouldn’t be surprised if they challenge you as well. We often think that if we had that man’s means or that man’s ability or that man’s opportunity, we could do something worth doing; but, as we are, there is no possibility of any great thing. Yet God does n",
   "content_zh": "赐予你恩惠 从上帝我们的父亲和主耶稣基督。 销售与交易今日的Kindle交易包括了\"旧约\",\"Proverbs\",\"忠实的存在\",\"蒂姆·凯勒的生活与影响\"等书籍,还有更多. Westminster Books通过提供ESV圣经的折扣以及Tyndale的新约500周年纪念版,继续他们的改造销售。 推荐读取主流如何为马诺斯圈招募。 Aaron Renn解释道“不对称的指责、高调的演讲和有选择地复活的规范正在驱使年轻人走向主流谴责的影响者。” 精神疾病是如何成为身份的。 迈尔斯·韦恩茨(英语:Myles Werntz)对弗雷德里克·德·博尔(英语:Fredri克·德·博尔)所著新书的一篇有趣的评论,解释了精神疾病是如何成为身份的. \" 21世纪的口腔疾病是一个日益扩大的类别 -- -- 一个日益由功能最强、因而可见的成员所支配的类别。 由我大学学生造成的严重精神病患者, 怎么会这样? 是否因为关闭传统精神病院, 是不是因为互联网驱动的由功能性很强的影响者自我诊断的现象? 精神病学作为一种职业的边缘化? 或者否认、浪漫化和政治?” 这里也有可能发生 “当欧洲许多国家发生暴乱时,美国许多人问道,“从许多方面讲,欧洲大陆是西方文明的摇篮。 ” 作为历史建筑、礼拜场所和商业财产在我们眼前燃起的夜晚新闻,我们如何理解这一点?” 卡尔·特鲁曼警告说,在欧洲发生的事情在美国也可能发生. 8 帮助你的孩子们爱教会的方法。 Shiphrah Lakka提供一系列方法来帮助你的孩子学会热爱教堂. “虽然家中的门徒活动极为重要,而且每个基督教家长都应该追求的东西,但它永远不能取代教会。 一起阅读《圣经》,作为一个家庭祈祷,以及在我们的家中教导我们的孩子了解上帝是关键的做法。 然而,上帝对信徒们的设计超出了我们家园的墙壁。 他叫我们属于一个信仰者社区,他们崇拜、服务和共同生活。” 我讨厌你的万圣节装饰 马克·西姆斯写下了今天万圣节的现实. “下次我出去时,我们将真正地慢下来,接受你设置的被蒙住的黑色人物在中间用假婴儿围住一个五角星,这样他就可以熟悉撒旦仪式和儿童祭祀。 我的意思是,他还能在哪里得到 这一重要的文化经验? 显然,你的印象是,变得对暴力和死亡不敏感是我们整个社区采取的重要一步——甚至庆祝。 在这里,暴躁的老马克(boo!)担心为什么我们的文化似乎更加渴望消遣死亡和恶魔——但你告诉我,这真的很有趣! 为我留一具假尸体!” 为何纸作\"活\". 丹尼尔·达林(Daniel Darling)解释自己对纸本书籍的持续热爱(即使他并不完全反对电子书籍). “当我在2 000多岁开始写作生涯时,每次我出席的写作会都发表严重警告。 电子书籍最终会接管。 纸上书是过去的事 图书馆是另一个时代的优秀文物. 但事实并非如此。 有价值的东西 Maltbie Davenport Babcock的这番话常常是对我的挑战, 我们常常认为,如果我们有那个人的手段,或者他的能力,或者他的机会,我们就可以做一些值得做的事;但是,正如我们一样,没有任何伟大的事情的可能性。 然而上帝却如此",
