   "title": "Digital doors open the gospel for islanders in Southeast Asia",
   "url": "https://www.imb.org/2026/10/05/digital-doors-open-the-gospel-for-islanders-in-southeast-asia/",
   "category": "missionary",
   "source": "IMB",
   "source_url": "https://www.imb.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-10",
   "summary": "Recently, an International Mission Board team in Southeast Asia asked a young woman if she had heard the story of Jesus. She replied that, yes, she had heard about Him through a video online! “Back in the day,” shared Amanda Clarkston, an IMB missionary who has served in Southeast Asia for 33 years, “when I first came on the field, you’d go somewhere and gather all the people together in the village to watch the JESUS film.” Now, face-to-face conversations about Christ on the Southeast Asian isl",
   "summary_zh": "最近,东南亚国际使团委员会的一个小组询问一名年轻妇女是否听说过耶稣的故事。 她回答说,是的,她通过网络视频听到了他的消息! “回到今天 ” , 分享了IMB在东南亚服役了33年的传教士阿曼达·克拉克斯顿(Amanda Clarkston ) , “ 当我第一次来到现场时,你会去一个地方,把村里的所有人聚集在一起观看JESUS电影。 ” 现在,面对面的谈论基督 在东南亚是。",
   "title_zh": "数字化之门为东南亚岛民打开福音之门",
   "content": "Just as young people today have become more comfortable with talking online than in person, the same is true for people in Southeast Asia. IMB missionaries are creating and publishing Jesus-focused ads, videos and other digital content to connect with the lost through the internet. IMB Photo Recently, an International Mission Board team in Southeast Asia asked a young woman if she had heard the story of Jesus. She replied that, yes, she had heard about Him through a video online! “Back in the day,” shared Amanda Clarkston, an IMB missionary who has served in Southeast Asia for 33 years, “when I first came on the field, you’d go somewhere and gather all the people together in the village to watch the JESUS film.” Now, face-to-face conversations about Christ on the Southeast Asian islands are harder to accomplish. While teams travel to these remote islands often, living in a sparsely populated, animistic background culture as a foreigner creates suspicion and make long-term ministry difficult. Furthermore, young people today have become more comfortable with talking online than they are in person, Clarkston said, which is true of the islanders as well. Attempting to have a spiritual conversation face-to-face has become “too much” for locals, Clarkston shared. So, how do you share the gospel with multiple people groups who are constantly online and less comfortable with in-person interactions? For these Southeast Asia teams, digital engagement — the use of social media platforms to share a message — has become a plausible and effective entry point. The social media agency We Are Social confirmed this, revealing that 82.4% of Southeast Asia’s population uses the internet. “No matter where they go, how far they go, how remote it is, people have phones,” Clarkston and her team realized, “And though sometimes they do have to climb up the highest peak to get reception, people do it.” Clarkston’s team has begun creating and publishing Jesus-focused ads, videos and other digital content in hopes of building bridges to the islanders through the internet. Viewers can click on the ad to message back and forth with a responder, a local believer or missionary who is available to pray, build relationships and answer spiritual questions. “It seems like locals are more open to watching those things in the privacy of their own cell phones,” Clarkston said. Clarkston intends to use digital engagement as a means for initial contact with people with animistic backgrounds, evangelism and, eventually, discipleship. She said that this new ministry has the potential to open doors with individuals across these islands who would normally never reach out on their own or respond to the gospel in person. “Maybe they’ll respond this way,” Clarkston said, “I know without a shadow of a doubt that God is calling people to Himself.” Now, more than ever, technology has a grip on society. Many spend hours each day mindlessly scrolling, searching for meaning, for happiness. And now, more than ever, there is an incredible opportunity to plant seeds across Southeast Asian islands through digital engagement. The IMB Southeast Asia team gives praise to the Lord that He has provided a creative way to reach the lost and plant seeds. Pray the people among the Southeast Asian islands would see these ads and engage with responders boldly, even though they may face persecution or harm because of it. Names were changed for security. Mikah Young is serving overseas with the IMB. The work of the IMB is sustained through faithful giving to the Cooperative Program and the Lottie Moon Christmas Offering ® . The Lottie Moon Christmas Offering ® is a registered trademark of Woman’s Missionary Union. The post Digital doors open the gospel for islanders in Southeast Asia appeared first on IMB .",
   "content_zh": "正如今天的年轻人对在线交谈比亲自交谈更加自在,东南亚人民也是如此。 IMB传教士正在创作并出版以耶稣为主的广告,视频等数字内容,以通过互联网与失落者相接. 最近,东南亚国际使团委员会的一个小组问一名年轻妇女是否听说过耶稣的故事。 她回答说,是的,她通过网络视频听到了他的消息! “回到今天 ” , 分享了IMB在东南亚服役了33年的传教士阿曼达·克拉克斯顿(Amanda Clarkston ) , “ 当我第一次来到现场时,你会去一个地方,把村里的所有人聚集在一起观看JESUS电影。 ” 现在,关于东南亚岛屿上的基督的面对面对话更难完成。 虽然各小组经常前往这些偏远岛屿,但作为外国人生活在人口稀少的厌世主义背景文化中,这造成了怀疑,使长期部委变得困难。 此外,克拉克斯顿说,今天的年轻人对在线交谈比他们本人感到更加自在,岛上居民也是如此。 Clarkston分享, 试图面对面进行精神对话, 所以,你如何与多个人群体分享福音呢? 他们经常在线,对亲身互动不太满意。 对于这些东南亚小组来说,数字参与——利用社交媒体平台分享信息——已成为一个可信而有效的切入点。 东南亚82.4%的人口使用互联网。 克拉克斯顿和她的团队意识到,“尽管有时他们必须爬上最高的山峰才能得到接待,但人们还是这么做了。” Clarkston的团队开始创作和发布以耶稣为焦点的广告,视频等数字内容,希望通过互联网为岛民搭起桥梁. 取景者可以点击广告,与回复者,当地信众或传教士相接来回留言,他们可以进行祈祷,建立关系并回答精神问题. Clarkston说, “当地人似乎更愿意在手机的隐私中观看这些东西。 克拉克斯顿打算用数字化的接战作为与有动画背景,福音派,并最终有门徒身份的人进行初步接触的手段. 她说,这个新的部有可能对这些岛屿上的个人敞开大门,他们通常不会独自伸出援手或亲自回应福音。 “也许他们会以这种方式回应,”克拉克斯顿说,“我毫不怀疑地知道,上帝正在号召人们投靠自己。 ” 现在,技术比以往更加控制社会。 许多人每天花上数小时无所顾忌地滚动,寻找意义,追求幸福. 现在,比以往任何时候,通过数字化参与,在东南亚各岛屿播种种子的机会比以往任何时候都多。 IMB东南亚队称赞了\"主\",他为到达失落地并播下种子提供了创造性的方法. 请东南亚各岛屿人民看到这些广告,并大胆地与回应者接触,尽管他们可能因此而面临迫害或伤害。 更改了安全名称。 米卡·杨在IMB海外服役. IMB的工作通过忠实地向合作方案和洛蒂·穆恩提供圣诞礼物来维持。 Lottie Moon圣诞献礼是女子传教联盟的注册商标。 Digital门打开东南亚岛民福音,",
   "image": "https://www.imb.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20251202MP1464web.jpg",
   "author": "Mikah Young",
   "tags": [
    "From the Field",
    "News",
    "digital engagement",
    "IMB",
    "International Mission Board",
    "Mikah Young",
    "Southeast Asia",
    "The Jesus film"
   ],
