   "fetched_at": "2026-11-11T00:26:09.549317",
   "extra": {
    "feed_type": "rss20"
   },
   "id": "06ca780dd276a64f"
  },
  {
   "title": "Training Oral Translators Across Southeast Asia",
   "url": "https://wycliffe.net/2026/08/12/training-oral-translators-across-southeast-asia/",
   "category": "missionary",
   "source": "Wycliffe",
   "source_url": "https://www.wycliffe.net/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "This project seeks to equip trainers who can contextualise and deliver OBT training within Latin America",
   "summary_zh": "该项目旨在为培训师提供能够在拉丁美洲范围内提供OBT培训的背景知识",
   "title_zh": "在东南亚培训口译员",
   "content": "A three-year training program will prepare local translators across Southeast Asia to put the Bible into spoken forms—like storytelling and song—for communities that share knowledge by voice, not writing. Three workshops will build translators’ skills from basic to advanced to mentoring, so at least 20 participants gain local expertise. Project Name: Training Oral Translators Across Southeast Asia Implementing Organization: Wycliffe Global Alliance Contact: Evelyn Gan Consultant for Oral Translation Programmes Wycliffe Global Alliance evelyn_gan@wycliffe.net Start date: FY 2026 End date: FY 2028 Summary Across Southeast Asia, many communities pass along their culture through spoken word—storytelling, song, and drama—rather than through reading and writing. For them, hearing the Bible in these natural forms often connects more deeply than a printed text. Oral Bible Translation is expanding rapidly in Southeast Asia, but the region lacks enough trained people to sustain it. Seminary graduates know the Bible but not oral translation. Practitioners already working need a path to advance their skills. And almost no one is ready to step into consultant roles. Without urgent, structured training, this shortage could stall Oral Bible Translation projects across the region. This three-year project will trains local translators and seminary students in oral Bible translation. Participants move through three stages: a foundation workshop, an advanced workshop and consultant-level training, with only those who show strong skills advancing to the next stage. Our goal is for at least 20 participants, with a smaller group becoming fully qualified to guide future translation projects. Half of the trainers will themselves be new, gaining experience so the program can continue and grow after this project ends. By working in collaboration with Wycliffe Thai Foundation, Wycliffe Malaysia, YWAM Chiang Mai, FCBH, Spoken Worldwide and CRU, the project is rooted in strong partnerships that will ensure sustainability and local ownership. Give to this Project Click Give Now to go to our secure giving portal. As you complete the form, you will be asked to ‘Choose a project’. Select Training Oral Translators Across Southeast Asia . Give Now Budget Total need (in USD): $147,277 Contributions received / pledged: $36,677 Balance needed: $110,600 To learn more about this funding opportunity, email Evelyn Gan, Consultant for Oral Translation Programmes, Wycliffe Global Alliance: evelyn_gan@wycliffe.net",
   "content_zh": "一个为期三年的培训方案将为东南亚各地的当地翻译提供准备,以便将《圣经》变成口头形式,如讲故事和作歌,供通过语音而不是写作分享知识的社区使用。 三个讲习班将培养笔译员的技能,从基本技能到高级技能再到指导技能,因此,至少有20名学员获得当地专门知识。 项目名称:在整个东南亚培训口笔译员 执行组织:怀克里夫全球联盟联系人:伊夫林甘口笔译方案顾问 Wycliffe全球联盟 Eviblyn gan@wycliffe.net 开始日期:2026财政年度 结束日期:东南亚2028财政年度摘要,许多社区通过口语——故事、歌曲和戏剧——而不是通过阅读和写作来传播其文化。 对他们来说,听到这些自然形态的\"圣经\"往往比印刷文本更深入地连接. 口语圣经翻译在东南亚正在迅速扩张,但该地区缺乏足够的训练有素的人来维持. 修道院毕业生知道\"圣经\",但不会口头翻译. 已经在工作的从业人员需要一条提高技能的道路。 几乎没有人愿意担任顾问。 如果不进行紧急、有条理的培训,这种短缺可能使整个区域的口语圣经翻译项目陷于停顿。 这个为期三年的项目将对当地翻译和神学院学生进行口语圣经翻译的培训. 与会者分三个阶段:基础讲习班、高级讲习班和顾问一级的培训,只有那些表现出强大技能的人才能进入下一阶段。 我们的目标是至少为20名参与者服务,人数较少的群体将完全有资格指导未来的翻译项目。 一半的训练员会自己是新手,获得经验,以便这个项目结束后方案能够继续并发展. 通过同Wycliffe Thai Foundation、Wycliffe Malaysia、YWAM Chiang Mai、FCBH、Spoken Worldwide和CRU合作,该项目植根于强有力的伙伴关系,将确保可持续性和地方所有权。 给这个工程 点击 现在给到我们的安全赠送门户。 填表时,您将被要求选择一个项目。 在整个东南亚选择培训口笔译员。 所需余额:110 600美元 为了了解更多有关这一资助机会的情况,电子邮件:Evelyn Gan, Wycliffe全球联盟口头翻译方案顾问:evelyn gan@wycliffe.net",
