  {
   "title": "Training Oral Translators in Indonesia",
   "url": "https://wycliffe.net/2026/08/12/training-oral-translators-in-indonesia/",
   "category": "missionary",
   "source": "Wycliffe",
   "source_url": "https://www.wycliffe.net/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "This project seeks to equip trainers who can contextualise and deliver OBT training within Latin America",
   "summary_zh": "该项目旨在为培训师提供能够在拉丁美洲范围内提供OBT培训的背景知识",
   "title_zh": "在印尼培训口译员",
   "content": "Indonesia has hundreds of languages still without Scripture in natural, spoken forms. This three-year program will train 20 local translators and seminary students to fill that gap, building skills from basic to advanced to mentoring. Working with local partners, it aims to grow into a lasting, homegrown training network. Project Name: Training Oral Translators in Indonesia Implementing Organization: Wycliffe Global Alliance Evelyn Gan Consultant for Oral Translation Programmes Wycliffe Global Alliance evelyn_gan@wycliffe.net Start date: FY 2026 End date: FY 2028 Summary Indonesia is home to hundreds of languages whose speakers pass on knowledge through spoken word rather than writing. Most still lack the Bible in a form that feels natural to hear. Oral Bible Translation is expanding quickly in Indonesia, but training hasn’t kept up—seminary graduates lack oral translation skills, and working practitioners have no path to grow or reach consultant-level readiness. Without urgent, structured training, projects across the country risk stalling. This three-year project trains local translators and seminary students to close that gap. Participants move through three stages—foundational, advanced and consultant-level training—with those who show strong skills advancing to the next stage. Our goal is for at least 20 participants, with a smaller group becoming fully qualified to guide future translation projects on their own. The project partners with several Indonesian organizations, including seminaries, so that this training becomes part of local theological education rather than a one-time effort. That partnership is central to the goal: building lasting, Indonesian-led capacity so that projects no longer depend on outside experts. Give to this Project Click Give Now to go to our secure giving portal. As you complete the form, you will be asked to ‘Choose a project’. Select Training Oral Translators in Indonesia . Give Now Budget Total need (in USD): $123,729 Contributions received / pledged: $40,100 Balance needed: $83,629 To learn more about this funding opportunity, email Evelyn Gan, Consultant for Oral Translation Programmes, Wycliffe Global Alliance: evelyn_gan@wycliffe.net",
   "content_zh": "印尼仍有上百种语言, 这个为期三年的方案将培训20名当地翻译和神学院学生来填补这一空白,培养从基础到高级到指导的技能。 它与当地伙伴合作,旨在发展成为一个持久的本土培训网络。 项目名称:在印度尼西亚培训口笔译员 执行组织: Wycliffe 全球联盟 Evelyn Gan 口笔译方案顾问 Wycliffe 全球联盟 Eviblyn gan@wycliffe.net 开始日期:2026财政年度 结束日期:2028财政年度 印度尼西亚有数百种语言,讲者通过口语而不是写作传递知识。 大多数人仍然缺乏一种自然而然的听觉形式的\"圣经\". 在印尼, 口语圣经翻译正在迅速扩展, 但训练没有保持下去, 没有紧急、有条理的培训,全国各地的项目就有可能停顿。 这个为期三年的项目培训当地翻译和神学院学生以弥合这一差距。 学员们经过三个阶段,即创始、高级和顾问一级的培训,那些表现出强大技能的人进入下一阶段。 我们的目标是让至少20名参与者参加,一个规模较小的团体完全有资格独自指导未来的翻译项目。 该项目与包括神学院在内的若干印度尼西亚组织结成伙伴,使这种培训成为当地神学教育的一部分,而不是一次性的努力。 这种伙伴关系是目标的核心:建立由印度尼西亚领导的持久能力,使项目不再依赖外部专家。 给这个工程 点击 现在给到我们的安全赠送门户。 填表时,您将被要求选择一个项目。 在印度尼西亚选择培训口笔译员。 所需总额(以美元计):123 729美元 为了了解更多有关这一资助机会的情况,电子邮件:Evelyn Gan, Wycliffe全球联盟口头翻译方案顾问:evelyn gan@wycliffe.net",
   "image": "https://wycliffe.net/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/cropped-logo.png",
   "author": "Otabil Arthur Otabil Arthur",
