  {
   "title": "Does Christianity Make Sense? On God, Evil, and the Ache (with Gavin Ortlund)",
   "url": "https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/podcasts/gospelbound/does-christianity-make-sense/",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "The Gospel Coalition",
   "source_url": "https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-08",
   "summary": "Gavin Ortlund joins Collin Hansen to discuss apologetics and why Christianity makes sense.",
   "summary_zh": "加文·奥特伦德（ Gavin Ortlund ）与科林·汉森（ Collin Hansen ）一起讨论了护教学以及基督教为什么有意义。",
   "title_zh": "基督教有意义吗？论上帝、邪恶和痛苦（与Gavin Ortlund合作）",
   "content": "Not long ago, my son asked me about all the people King David killed in 2 Samuel 8. We’ve been reading through that book during family devotions before bed. He’s right to be disturbed. So we had a conversation about why he’s unnerved, how we develop moral instincts, and how we’d respond to someone who rejects God because of these and similar accounts in the Old Testament. We did apologetics together. As he gets a little older, I’ll point him toward the YouTube channel of my friend Gavin Ortlund, who does an excellent job of answering many hard questions about Christianity and the Bible. Then, a few years later, I’ll point him to Gavin’s books, including his latest, Why Christianity Makes Sense: A Book About Jesus, the Mysteries of the World, and the Longings in Your Heart (Zondervan Reflective). He’s back on Gospelbound to discuss all things apologetics, from the multiverse, to slavery, to morality as merely a taste for sugar, to winning the lottery 10 billion times in a row. In This Episode 00:00 – Why people may be more open to spiritual answers today 03:36 – “The ache” and the longing for transcendence 09:29 – What about Christianity makes the least sense to Gavin? 11:39 – The problem of evil and the limits of tidy answers 19:09 – The growing challenge of divine hiddenness 24:34 – Fine-tuning and the odds of a life-permitting universe 32:07 – Is morality without God just a matter of taste? 37:25 – Slavery, the Bible, and the Christian roots of human equality 42:23 – Why fulfilled prophecy surprised Gavin 48:00 – What apologetic questions should Christians prepare for next? Resources Mentioned: Why Christianity Makes Sense by Gavin Ortlund Mere Christianity by C. S. Lewis Making Sense of God by Timothy Keller The Reason for God by Timothy Keller The Brothers Karamazov by Fyodor Dostoevsky Bullies and Saints by John Dickson Dominion by Tom Holland Gavin Ortlund’s YouTube channel, “ Truth Unites “ The Keller Center for Cultural Apologetics SIGN UP for my newsletter, Unseen Things . Help The Gospel Coalition renew and unify the contemporary church in the ancient gospel: Donate today . Don’t miss an episode of Gospelbound with Collin Hansen: Apple Podcasts Spotify YouTube TGC Updates",
   "content_zh": "不久前,我儿子问我 大卫国王在塞缪尔8号杀死的所有人 我们一直读那本书, 他有权被打扰。 因此,我们讨论了为什么他不紧张,我们如何发展道德本能,以及我们如何回应因旧约中这些和类似说法而拒绝上帝的人。\n\n我们一起做杂耍 我将指向我的朋友Gavin Ortlund的YouTube频道,\n\n然后,几年后,我将指给他看加文的书籍,包括他的最新著作《基督教为什么讲道理:关于耶稣的书》、《世界的谜》和《你心中的长寿》。 他回到福音书上,讨论所有的事情,从多语言,到奴隶制,再到道德,仅仅作为糖味,再到连续100亿次中奖。\n\n在这部第00:00集里, 为什么人们可能更开放 精神答案今天03:36, “痛”和渴望超越 09:29, 基督教对加文来说最没有意义吗?\n\n11:39 – 邪恶问题和整洁的极限回答 19:09 – 神圣隐秘的日益严峻的挑战 24:34 – 精细调整和生命空间的几率 32:07 – 没有上帝的道德是不是只是品味问题?\n\n37:25 — — 奴隶制,圣经,以及人类平等的基督教根源 42:23 — — 为什么满足预言让加文惊奇 4800 — — 基督徒应该为下一个问题准备什么呢? 资源参考:Gavin Ortlund Mere Christian 著 C. S.\n\n由Timothy Keller主演 Timothy Keller The Brothers Karamazov主演 Fyodor Dostoevsky 欺凌和圣徒 由John Dickson Dominion主演 Tom Holland Gavin Ortlund 的YouTube频道 \" 真理团结 \" , Keller文化学中心为我的通讯 \" 不明事物 \" 配音。\n\n帮助 福音联盟在古代福音中更新并统一了当代教会:今天捐赠. 不要错过带Collin Hansen的福音:苹果播客Spotify YouTube TGC更新",
   "image": "https://media.thegospelcoalition.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/23121942/196.-thumbnail-1.png",
   "author": "Collin Hansen, Gavin Ortlund",
