   "published": "2026-11-04",
   "summary": "Many Christians are most committed to their local church. A subset has strong feelings of loyalty toward a denomination. It seems unlikely that commitment to something as nebulous as “evangelicalism” is the animating principle for many. Perhaps it is time to use the word only as an adjective, describing a cluster of shared traits, or...  Continue Reading",
   "summary_zh": "许多基督徒最致力于他们的当地教会. 一个子集对一个教派有强烈的忠诚感. 对许多人来说,对“福音派”这样模糊的东西的承诺似乎不可能是动画原则。 也许是时候把这个词仅仅用作形容词,描述一组共同的特征,或者. 继续阅读",
   "title_zh": "福音主义存在吗？",
