   "summary": "When Anna Dunsbergen enrolled at the University of Northern Iowa (UNI) as a freshman, she planned to become a teacher, not a worship leader. In high school, she had sung in both school and church choirs, and had some basic guitar skills, but didn’t aspire to serve as a church musician. Her mom had led  Read more...   The post  Churches Face a Shortage of Worship Leaders  appeared first on  Christianity Today .",
   "summary_zh": "当安娜·邓斯贝根(英语:Anna Dunsbergen)在北爱荷华大学(英语:Northern Iowa University (UNI))注册为新生时,她计划成为一名教师,而不是崇拜领袖. 高中时,她在学校和教会合唱团都唱过歌,并拥有一些基本的吉他技巧,但并不想担任教会音乐家. 她妈妈领导了更多的读者...\n\n教会面对宗教领袖的短缺,",
