   "title": "This Week in Christian Books (November 3, 2026)",
   "url": "https://www.challies.com/resources/this-week-in-christian-books-november-3-2026/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Tim Challies",
   "source_url": "https://www.challies.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-10",
   "summary": "Tuesday is the day most publishers release their new books. Here is a look at the Christian books that came our way this week, including Prodigal Culture, Scroll Less Live More, and a graphic novel of Pilgrim's Progress. See Also New and Notable Christian Books for October 2026 (Plus a Preview of November) This Week in Christian Books (October 27, 2026) Best Commentaries on Leviticus",
   "summary_zh": "星期二是大多数出版商发行新书的日子. 以下是本周我们走过的基督教书籍, 包括《Prodigal Culture》、《Scroll Less Live More》和《朝圣者的进步》的绘画小说。 也见2026年10月的基督教新书和著名书籍(Plus a preview of 11月的预览) 本周的基督教书籍(2026年10月27日) 关于利维提库斯的最佳评论",
   "title_zh": "本周基督教书籍（ 2026年11月3日）",
   "content": "Tuesday is the day most Christian publishers release their new books, so each week I let you know what has just come our way from the publishers I follow most closely. This week brings Andrew Walker’s diagnosis of our prodigal culture, a graphic-novel edition of The Pilgrim’s Progress , and Samuel James’s Scroll Less, Live More . On the academic side, you will find reference works and commentaries. You may also want to consider Trevin Wax’s liturgy for daily prayer. For each book, I’ve included the publisher’s description and its list of endorsers. Books for Everyone Crossway Prodigal Culture A People in Ruins and the Way Back Home Andrew T. Walker Endorsed by: R. Albert Mohler Jr., Carl R. Trueman, Allie Beth Stuckey, Seth Dillon, and Kristen Waggoner Publisher’s description We have forgotten what it means to be human. American men and women are feeling the despair of a counterfeit culture, one where polarization has replaced conversation, pornography is chosen over true intimacy, and marriage and family are postponed indefinitely. The resulting isolation has forced us to confront the truth: individualism and worldly systems cannot take the place of God’s design for humanity. This scholarly yet accessible study examines the effects of secularism, nihilism, and barbarism on culture today, and explains why a biblical worldview is essential for human flourishing. Andrew T. Walker skillfully confronts 10 pressing issues—including loneliness, sexual confusion, anti-institutionalism, and identity. Affirming that shared norms grounded in creation order are the solution to social decline, he champions a return to biblical standards of freedom, human nature, and purpose. Walker compares Western culture to the prodigal son in Scripture—a culture that has squandered its inheritance and must now decide whether it will return to the Father or continue living in squalor. Buy it at Amazon or Westminster Books . Crossway Scroll Less, Live More 10 Healthy Tech Habits for Teens Samuel D. James Endorsed by: Paul David Tripp, Matt Smethurst, and Whitney Newby Publisher’s description Nearly every teenager carries a smartphone in their pocket. What was once an innocent tool, providing a quick escape and a promise of connection, has now become a world that holds us captive. Looking up from the tiny pixels and refraining from the incessant scrolling may be the rest that our souls need. Scroll Less, Live More offers teens and families 10 practical habits for navigating the world of technology from a Christian perspective. From the author of the Christian Book Award winner, Digital Liturgies, tech-realist Samuel James applies his ideas into action steps to help teenagers keep digital tools in their proper place. By addressing how technology affects our social interactions, sleep patterns, critical thinking, and much more, James helps readers see the wisdom in God’s perfect design and, as a result, resist the temptations prevalent in the smartphone age. Buy it at Amazon or Westminster Books . Zondervan Get to Work Seeing Your Daily Grind as God’s Good Gift Jonny Ardavanis Endorsed by: R. Kent Hughes, R. Albert Mohler, Jr., Allie Beth Stuckey, and Colby Parkinson Publisher’s description Learn to avoid both passivity and burnout by discovering God’s glorious design for work—and how to labor, rest, and steward your time in ways that glorify God and maximize your joy. The average person will spend 90,000 hours working—a staggering third of their life. For many, these hours feel like a necessary burden, something we have to do. But what if work isn’t a punishment to endure, but a privilege to embrace—a divine “get to” rather than a grim “got to”? In a time of contradictory messages about work, hurry, and rest, pastor and author Jonny Ardavanis dives into Scripture to help you see work as a divine calling, guiding you to partner with God and find profound meaning and purpose in your daily work, whether you’re a plumber, a CEO, or a stay-at-home mom. Get to W",
   "content_zh": "星期二是大多数基督教出版商发行新书的一天,所以每个星期我都会让大家知道,我最密切地关注的出版商,我们刚刚走过了什么路。 本周安德鲁·沃克(Andrew Walker)对我们浪子文化的诊断,\n\n在学术方面,你会找到参考著作和评论. 您可能也想参考Trevin Wax的礼拜。 每本书我都包括出版商的描述及其认可者名单。 为所有人出版的书 《十字路口的浪荡文化 A Ruins》 和《回家之路》 Andrew T. Walker 由R. Albert Mohler Jr., Carl R.\n\nTrueman、Allie Beth Stuckey、Seth Dillon和Kristen Waggoner出版社的描述 我们忘记了人类的意义。 美国男女都感受到了假冒文化的绝望,这种文化的两极分化取代了对话,色情作品被选择而不是真正的亲密,婚姻和家庭被无限期推迟.\n\n由此产生的孤立迫使我们面对真理:个人主义和世界制度不能取代上帝对人类的设计。 这份学术性但易于获取的研究审查了世俗主义、虚无主义和野蛮主义对当今文化的影响,并解释了为什么圣经世界观对人类繁荣至关重要。 安德鲁·T.\n\nWalker巧妙地面对10个紧迫问题——包括孤独、性混乱、反机构主义和身份认同。 他申明,基于创造秩序的共同准则是解决社会衰退的办法,他支持恢复自由、人性和宗旨的圣经标准。\n\nWalker将西方文化与圣经中的浪子相提并论——一种浪费了遗产的文化,现在必须决定是回到父亲身边还是继续生活在肮脏之中。 在亚马逊或威斯敏斯特书店买的 Crossway Scroll Less, Live More 10 Health Tech Habits for Teens Samuel D. 互联网档案馆的存檔,存档日期2013-12-02., p.\n\n由保罗·大卫·特里普(Paul David Trip),马特·斯梅特赫斯特(Matt Smethurst)和惠特尼·纽比(Whitney Newby)出版社(Whitney Newby Publishers)的描述所认可,几乎每个青少年口袋里都有智能手机. 曾经是无辜的工具,提供了快速逃脱和联系的保证,现在已经成为束缚我们的世界。 从细微的像素上看 避免不断的滚动 可能是我们的灵魂需要的其余部分\n\nScroll Less, Live More为青少年和家庭提供了10种实用的习惯,从基督教的角度探索技术世界. 从克里斯蒂安图书奖得主Digital Liturgies的作者,技术现实主义者塞缪尔·詹姆斯(Samuel James)将他的想法运用到行动步骤中,帮助青少年将数字工具放在合适的位置.\n\n通过探讨技术如何影响我们的社会互动、睡眠模式、批判性思维,以及更多,詹姆斯帮助读者在上帝的完美设计中看到智慧,从而抵御智能手机时代流行的诱惑。 在亚马逊或威斯敏斯特书店买的 Zondervan Get to Work 将《每日工作报》视为上帝的好礼物Jonny Ardavanis,\n\nAlbert Mohler, Jr., Allie Beth Stuckey, 以及Colby Parkinson Publishers的描述, 学会通过发现上帝的光荣的工作设计来避免被动和疲惫, 以及如何以赞美上帝的方式劳动、休息和支配你的时间, 平均工作时间为90 000小时,占其生命的惊人的三分之一。\n\n对于许多人来说,这些小时感觉像一个必要的负担,我们必须做的事情。 如果工作不是忍耐的惩罚, 而是接受神圣的“得到”而不是残忍的“必须”的特权呢?\n\n在工作、匆忙、休息、牧师、作家Jonny Ardavanis潜入圣经, 帮助你将工作视为神圣的召唤, 引导你与上帝合作, 到达W",
