  {
   "title": "The Tyranny of Preferences",
   "url": "https://rss.desiringgod.org/link/10732/17512370/the-tyranny-of-preferences",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "Desiring God",
   "source_url": "https://www.desiringgod.org/blog.rss",
   "published": "2026-11-06",
   "summary": "Desires are funny things. They drive everything we do, and yet, like the engine in a car, we rarely look at them. As the Book says, man’s heart is deep water and all that. But wise men, like C.S. Lewis, pop the hood and force us to inspect the desires that move us. In  The Screwtape Letters , he shows how our pinings and preferences can subtly erode peace and crowd out love if left unexamined. Lewis diagnoses the disease of preferences gone wild, exposing the disharmony that results when diminut",
   "summary_zh": "欲望是有趣的东西。 他们开着我们做的一切, 然而,就像汽车里的引擎一样, 我们很少看到他们。 正如《圣经》所说,人的心是深水。 但聪明人,像C. S. Lewis, 打开引擎盖,强迫我们检查 移动我们的欲望。 在\"斯克丽丝塔普信条\"中,他展示了我们的针锋相对和偏好如何会潜伏地侵蚀和平,并且如果不加考量地排挤爱情.\n\n刘易斯诊断出偏好病变得疯狂 暴露出当Diminut导致的不和谐",
   "title_zh": "偏好的暴政",
   "content": "Desires are funny things. They drive everything we do, and yet, like the engine in a car, we rarely look at them. As the Book says, man’s heart is deep water and all that. But wise men, like C.S. Lewis, pop the hood and force us to inspect the desires that move us. In The Screwtape Letters , he shows how our pinings and preferences can subtly erode peace and crowd out love if left unexamined. Lewis diagnoses the disease of preferences gone wild, exposing the disharmony that results when diminutive wants grow into systematic demands — all to the tune of “Can’t you just . . . ?” ‘All-I-Want’ State of Mind In Letter 17, the demon Screwtape describes an old woman who struggles with the sin of gluttony, not from overeating but from being overdemanding with her preferences. At table after table, she rejects the meal offered to her “with a demure little sigh,” insisting that all she wants is “a cup of tea properly made, or an egg properly boiled, or a slice of bread properly toasted” ( The Screwtape Letters , 88). Because her requests are singular and relatively small, she fools herself into thinking them reasonable and easy to accommodate, even though they conceal “an insatiable demand for the exact” (89). She refuses to feast until her foibles are indulged. Lewis dubs this the “‘All-I-want’ state of mind,” where one particular preference comes to dominate. Like a totalitarian dictator, the singular all controls everything and everyone. As a result, the old woman infects every table she pulls up to with “querulousness, impatience, uncharitableness, and self-concern” (87). Under the guise of “All-I-want,” she is a micro-tyrant, “a positive terror” to everyone around her (87). Her petite preferences sabotage the spiritual health of her community — and the demons love it. Tiny Tyrannies The danger of an “All-I-want” mentality extends far beyond eating. Consider how many approach the church the same way this woman approaches the table. We bring seemingly small desires with us, expressed (at first) as slight requests: Can’t you just be a bit more like me? Can’t you just let the Spirit lead more? All I want is some newer music. Like the old woman, we fool ourselves into thinking these preferences should be easy to accommodate because we present them solo, not as a list of demands. But even virtuous desires, isolated from other goods, go a bit mad, becoming lone judges over everyone and everything. Almost without our noticing, “All-I-want” preferences become tiny tyrannies. Consider two examples. In the Old Testament, God miraculously fed his people in the wilderness with manna (cf. Exodus 16). Each morning, bread fell from heaven to meet all their dietary needs. God laid the table with bespoke portions so that each individual left satisfied. But the Israelites let little preferences grow into sinful demands. They missed meat — nothing wrong with that. But they let that desire fester and grow worms. You can imagine them sliding the proffered plate of manna away “with a demure little sigh” and thinking, All I want is the teeniest, weeniest bit of charred steak. Left unchecked, their preferences led to grumbling, ingratitude, and scorning the meal God offered. In the New Testament, we see something similar in the church at Thyatira (Revelation 2:18–29). King Jesus commends their works of love, faith, and patience, which increase day by day. And yet he confronts them because they “tolerate that woman Jezebel, who calls herself a prophetess and is teaching and seducing my servants to practice sexual immorality” (Revelation 2:20). How could a faithful church allow such depravity? The text doesn’t tell us explicitly, but likely the preferences of a fussy few dominated the many. Can’t you just allow this woman to teach occasionally? She’s so dynamic. Or, All I want is that she preach once a month. Can’t you just give her a mic? Or, Can’t we just do something new? This woman’s novelty is so refreshing . Perhaps not everyone at Thyatira indulged he",
   "content_zh": "欲望是有趣的东西。 他们开着我们做的一切, 然而,就像汽车里的引擎一样, 我们很少看到他们。 正如《圣经》所说,人的心是深水。 但聪明人,像C. S. Lewis, 打开引擎盖,强迫我们检查 移动我们的欲望。 在\"斯克丽丝塔普信条\"中,他展示了我们的针锋相对和偏好如何会潜伏地侵蚀和平,并且如果不加考量地排挤爱情.\n\n刘易斯诊断出偏好病已经发狂,揭露了当Diminutive想要成长为系统性要求时所造成的不和谐,这些要求都与 \" 你就不能只是.? \" 的 \" All-I-Want \" 的心态状态有关。 在17号信里,恶魔Screwtape描述了一个老妇人,她与过量食用,而不是因过度要求自己的偏好而挣扎。\n\n在一桌后,她拒绝向她提供的饭菜“含着一股谦卑的气息”,坚持说,她想要的只是“适当制成的茶杯,或适当煮好的鸡蛋,或适当烤好的面包片”(The Screwtape Letters,88)。\n\n由于她的请求是单数和相对小的,她自欺欺人地认为这些请求合理和容易满足,尽管这些请求掩盖了“对准确性的无厌要求”(89)。 她拒绝宴会,直到她被放纵 Lewis将此称为 \" 所有我渴望的 \" 心态,\n\n像一个极权独裁者一样,独一统统控制着一切和每个人. 结果,这个老妇人感染了她拉到的每张桌子,上面写着“自信、不耐烦、不慈悲和自顾”(87)。 她以“我渴望一切”为幌子,是对她周围所有人(87)的“积极的恐怖”。\n\n她的宠物偏好破坏了她的社区的精神健康——恶魔们也喜欢它. 小暴君们 “万能”心态的危险远远不止于吃东西。 想想有多少人走近教堂 就像这个女人走近桌子一样 我们带着看来很小的欲望,他们最初只是小声地要求: 你就不能更像我一点吗?\n\n为何不能让精神领导更多呢? 我只想要些新的音乐 和老妇人一样,我们自欺欺人地认为这些偏好应该容易适应,因为我们提出这些偏好是独奏的,而不是作为要求的清单. 但即使是良性欲望, 孤立于其他商品之外, 变得有点疯狂, 成为孤独的法官 凌驾于每个人和一切之上。\n\n几乎没有我们注意,“我完全希望”的偏好就变成了微小的暴政。 考虑两个例子。 在旧约中,上帝奇迹般地用甘露喂养他在荒野中的人民(参见Exodus 16). 每天早上,面包从天堂掉下来,以满足他们的饮食需求. 真主使桌子上摆满了标语,以便每个人都满意。\n\n但以色列人却很少偏好变成罪恶的要求。 他们错过了肉类——没有问题。 但是,他们让这种欲望腐烂 并生长蠕虫。 你可以想象,他们把甘露的盘子“带着一股谦虚的气息”滑走,并且想,我所想要的只是最年轻、最微弱的烧焦牛排。\n\n他们的偏好没有受到控制,导致他们抱怨、忘恩负义、蔑视上帝提供的餐食。 在新约中,我们在Thyatira的教堂里看到类似的东西(Revelation 2:18–29). 耶稣国王称赞他们的爱情,信仰和耐心的作品,这些作品每天都在增加.\n\n然而,他却与她们对抗,因为他们“把那个自称为先知的Jezebel的女人说成是先知,正在教导和引诱我的仆人进行性不道德的行为”(Revelation 2:20)。 忠诚的教会怎么会允许这种堕落? 文中并没有明确地告诉我们, 你就不能让这个女人偶尔教书吗?\n\n她非常活跃。 或者,我只要她每月传教一次 你就不能给她个麦克风吗? 我们就不能做点新的事情吗? 这个女人的新奇奇奇奇特, 也许不是每个人 在Thyatira 纵容他",
   "image": "https://dg.imgix.net/resources/17935/media/d8960274-7201-4e80-8893-b88b93e6504e/landscape/the-tyranny-of-preferences-en.png?ts=1793363483&ixlib=rails-4.3.1&fit=crop&w=2000&h=1050",
