  {
   "title": "Worldliness and the Friendship of God",
   "url": "https://rss.desiringgod.org/link/10732/17511238/worldliness-and-the-friendship-of-god",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "Desiring God",
   "source_url": "https://www.desiringgod.org/blog.rss",
   "published": "2026-11-05",
   "summary": "If you’re a faithful follower of Jesus today, try this experiment: Imagine that in five years you have completely walked away from Jesus.   You’re not questioning or struggling or arguing anymore. You’re not wrestling with whether to stay or leave the church. You never open the Bible. You have almost no impulse to pray. You’re shutting out anyone and everyone who wants to talk about God. You’re just gone. All the way  gone .   I hope it feels horrible, even unimaginable. I’m not exaggerating whe",
   "summary_zh": "如果你今天是耶稣的忠实追随者,请尝试这个实验: 想象五年后你完全离开了耶稣 你不再质疑或争吵。 你们不是在争先恐后, 你从来没有打开圣经。 你几乎没有祈祷的冲动。 任何想谈论上帝的人,\n\n你刚刚走了。 一直不见了。 我希望这感觉可怕,甚至难以想象。 我没有夸大其词",
   "title_zh": "世俗与神的友谊",
   "content": "If you’re a faithful follower of Jesus today, try this experiment: Imagine that in five years you have completely walked away from Jesus. You’re not questioning or struggling or arguing anymore. You’re not wrestling with whether to stay or leave the church. You never open the Bible. You have almost no impulse to pray. You’re shutting out anyone and everyone who wants to talk about God. You’re just gone. All the way gone . I hope it feels horrible, even unimaginable. I’m not exaggerating when I say nothing worse could happen to you (Revelation 14:11). If you’re honest in this hypothetical horror, what do you suspect might have led you away? What could have possibly drowned your once-strong love for Jesus? You might immediately assume some stubborn sin, or an especially painful relationship, or something in the Bible that never sat right with you. Sadly, souls discard Jesus every day for all kinds of awful reasons. If you forced yourself to list a dozen serious threats to your faith, would you think to list the risk of worldliness ? Do you ever fear that you would love this world too much to keep loving Jesus? Too few of us fear enough. Could You Be Demas? We know how dangerous worldliness can be because God gave us Demas. He inspired the apostle Paul to report, “Demas, in love with this present world, has deserted me” (2 Timothy 4:10). Demas once seemed to be an unusually strong, devoted, and fruitful lover of Jesus (Colossians 4:14) — a bold and effective minister of the gospel! — but he kept nibbling at the wrong buffets. And as he nibbled, an unholy hunger grew and grew until he spat Jesus out of his mouth. Paul watched his once-close friend die by short-lived pleasure. Worldliness is loving what the world loves at the expense of what God loves. Sometimes, worldliness is a love for something bad — drunkenness, gossip, violence, pornography. Often, it’s a distorted and disproportionate love for something good — family, food, career, sex. The unbelieving world loves those things, but in ways that defy God and deface all he loves — his word, his Son, his church. Do you love any calling, hobby, or relationship in such a way that it has started to erode the most important loves? Do you see hints of Demas’s descent anywhere in your life? Do you find your thought life being devoured by work? Do you spend hours and hours with your family and rarely talk about Jesus? Do you never miss your favorite show, but you struggle to find time to pray? Do you drag your feet to get to church and rush home to catch the game? Jesus warns us about the seed that falls among the thorns of worldliness: “They are those who hear the word, but the cares of the world and the deceitfulness of riches and the desires for other things enter in and choke the word, and it proves unfruitful” (Mark 4:18–19). He’s describing soul suffocation — the sharp tentacles of worldliness slowly wrapping themselves around a heart and strangling out hope, joy, and love. It’s horrifying. Why would anyone ever let that happen? Because Satan knows all too well how to make worldly anxieties seem bigger than God (Matthew 4:2–3), and he schemes to make earthly pleasures seem sweeter than God (Genesis 3:4–5). “This world is all that really matters,” he whispers. And if we believe him, we end up wanting the world God made — but hold the God, please. Four Dangers of Worldliness When this temptation comes — and it will come — will we cave and run like Demas, or will we fight for the only love that will truly satisfy? God arms us to face the deadly thorns: Do not love the world or the things in the world. If anyone loves the world, the love of the Father is not in him. For all that is in the world — the desires of the flesh and the desires of the eyes and pride of life — is not from the Father but is from the world. And the world is passing away along with its desires, but whoever does the will of God abides forever. (1 John 2:15–17) Do not love the world. Worldliness, these verses tea",
   "content_zh": "如果你今天是耶稣的忠实追随者,请尝试这个实验: 想象五年后你完全离开了耶稣 你不再质疑或争吵。 你们不是在争先恐后, 你从来没有打开圣经。 你几乎没有祈祷的冲动。 任何想谈论上帝的人,\n\n你刚刚走了。 一直不见了。 我希望这感觉可怕,甚至难以想象。 我并没有夸张, 如果你在这种假想的恐怖中诚实, 还有什么能淹没你曾经对耶稣的爱?\n\n你可能立即承担一些固执的罪过, 或一种特别痛苦的关系, 或者圣经中从未与你同在的东西。 可悲的是,灵魂每天都以各种可怕的理由抛弃耶稣. 如果你强迫自己 列出十几个严重的威胁 你的信仰, 你会考虑 列出 世界的风险?\n\n你是否曾担心过你会太爱这个世界 不再爱耶稣? 我们中恐惧的人太少了 你能成为德马斯吗? 我们知道世界有多危险 因为上帝给了我们德马斯 他激励使徒保罗报告说,“德马斯爱上了这个现在的世界,抛弃了我”(Timothy 4:10)。\n\n德马斯曾经似乎是耶稣的异常强壮,执着,富有成果的爱人(Colosians 4:14)——一位勇敢而有效的福音大臣! ——但他却不停地在错误的自助餐上抱怨. 当他吞咽时,不祥的饥饿逐渐增长,直到他吐出耶稣的嘴. 保罗看着他曾经亲密的朋友死于短暂的快乐.\n\n世界是爱世界所爱 牺牲上帝所爱 有时,世界性是对一些坏东西的热爱——醉酒,八卦,暴力,色情. 这往往是一种扭曲和不相称的对美好事物的爱——家庭、食物、职业、性。 不信世的人们喜欢那些东西,但是却以藐视上帝和诋毁他所爱的一切的方式——他的话,他的儿子,他的教堂.\n\n你是否喜欢任何电话、爱好或关系 以至于它开始侵蚀最重要的爱? Demas在一生中, 你发现你的思想生活被工作吞噬了吗? 你和家人一起呆上好几个小时 很少谈论耶稣? 你从来没有错过你最喜欢的节目, 但你努力寻找时间祈祷?\n\n你拖着脚去教堂 赶回家接球吗? 耶稣警告我们,世界的荆棘中落下的种子是:“他们就是那些听话的人,但世界的关心和财富的欺骗性以及对其他事物的欲望进入并扼杀这个词,这证明是不果实的”(Mark 4:18-19)。\n\n他描述灵魂窒息 — — 世界的尖锐触角慢慢地包围着心,扼杀希望、喜悦和爱。 这太可怕了。 为什么有人会让这种事发生? 因为撒旦非常了解如何使世界的焦虑看起来比上帝大(Matthew 4:2–3),他计划使地球的快乐看起来比上帝更甜(Genesis 3:4–5).\n\n“这个世界才是真正重要的。” 如果我们相信他,我们最终希望得到上帝创造的世界——但请抓住上帝。 世界的四种危险 当这种诱惑到来时——它将到来时——我们是否会像德马斯那样洞穴和奔跑,还是我们将为真正满足的唯一爱而斗争? 上帝让我们面对致命的刺: 不爱世间或世间物.\n\n若有人爱世间,则父之爱不在他. 因为世上的一切——肉体的欲望和眼睛的欲望和生命的骄傲——不是来自父亲,而是来自世界. 世界正在随其欲望而逝去,但谁遵循真主的旨意,谁将永居其中。 (约翰: 2:15-17) 不爱世间. 世界,这些诗歌茶",
   "image": "https://dg.imgix.net/resources/17930/media/c3bca6b2-429e-4bb4-9a63-8d3995c2e2e1/landscape/worldliness-and-the-friendship-of-god-en.png?ts=1791908180&ixlib=rails-4.3.1&fit=crop&w=2000&h=1050",
