  {
   "title": "A La Carte (November 5)",
   "url": "https://www.challies.com/a-la-carte/a-la-carte-november-5-2026/",
   "category": "giant",
   "source": "Tim Challies",
   "source_url": "https://www.challies.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "When you feel guilty about your giving / The missing piece in John Mark Comer’s quiet time / A manifesto for phone-free church / The pull of Rome / 4 Misconceptions about spiritual warfare / Slouching toward Narnia / Kindle deals, and more See Also A La Carte (June 27) Weekend A La Carte (October 25) Kindle Deals for Christian Readers",
   "summary_zh": "当您对自己的奉献感到内疚时/约翰·马克·科默（ John Mark Comer ）的安静时光中缺失的一部分/免费电话教堂的宣言/罗马的吸引力/对精神战的4种误解/对纳尼亚/Kindle优惠的懒散态度等另请参阅单点菜肴（ 6月27日）周末单点菜肴（ 10月25日）基督教读者的Kindle优惠",
   "title_zh": "点菜（ 11月5日）",
   "content": "May the Lord be with you and bless you today, my friends. Sales & Deals Today’s Kindle deals include a couple of Christmas devotionals, a Greg Koukl classic, and Seth Lewis’s Dream Small , among others. In case it’s of interest, Audible continues to offer a great deal—three months of service plus a $20 bonus for $0.99/month. You can unsubscribe at any time. Recommended Reading A Manifesto for Phone-Free Church. This article offers a lot to think about when it comes to the consequences of using our phones in church. “Distractions in worship will be with us always, but that does not mean we ought to go out into the highways and the hedges and invite as many distractions as possible. And here, we should note that there are good distractions in church—I am thinking of those babies that cry and fuss and laugh at all the wrong moments. Good distractions remind us that church is more than our personal ‘alone time’ with God. We are part of a family.” The Missing Piece in John Mark Comer’s Quiet Time. I think Matthew Bingham’s review of John Mark Comer’s book is bang on in both what it praises and what it criticizes. “Though Comer identifies as a Protestant, he relies on numerous quotations from ‘desert fathers and mothers,’ medieval mystics, and modern Roman Catholic and Eastern Orthodox theologians to justify his cafeteria approach to spirituality. As in his previous work, he engages with few heirs of the Reformation. Comer insists that Scripture is essential, but, for him, it doesn’t stand alone. Consistent with this non-Protestant mystical tradition, the book strongly emphasizes subjective, immediate communication from God apart from God’s inspired words in Scripture.” Free Chick-fil-A For a Year. Did you know that Midwestern Seminary is home to Spurgeon College, which is an undergraduate school that exists to equip students for the Kingdom? This November, they’re giving away a year’s supply of Chick-fil-A! Head over here to enter to win and discover other opportunities to grow deeper in Christ this month! (Sponsored) The Pull of Rome and the Promise of Grace. Chris Castaldo writes about those who are drawn to Rome. “A member of your small group confesses, seemingly out of the blue, that he’s been attending Mass. Next, you hear a deacon wonder aloud if we really needed to break with Rome. Then a family member announces that she has ‘crossed the Tiber,’ meaning she has converted to Roman Catholicism. Such conversations seem to be happening with greater frequency in Protestant circles. But why?” 4 Misconceptions About Spiritual Warfare. Costi Hinn outlines four fairly common misconceptions about spiritual warfare. “There is a short list of Christian beliefs that have as much mystery as spiritual warfare. While some things are really clear in the Bible regarding demons and demonic activity, there is a supernatural element to the unseen realm that humbles even the most educated theological student! At the same time, it seems that many people have a variety of opinions based on their experiences, which is not necessarily a negative thing, but it can lead to a lot of misconceptions.” Slouching Toward Narnia. Personally I’ve been enjoying reading all the different perspectives on the growing information we have about the forthcoming Narnia film(s). I think Nicholas McDonald’s article is one of the best so far. He explains his formula for a successful film adaptation (Faithfulness to Theme + Thoughtful Innovations = Great Film Adaptation) and tells whether he’s feeling hopeful as he considers The Magician’s Nephew in that way. Four Corrections to Make When You Feel Guilty About Your Giving. I think most people feel guilty about their giving from time to time. When that’s true of you, here are some ways you can correct the way you think and act. What I’m Enjoying Every week I ask the readers of this site to tell me what they are enjoying and, therefore, what they recommend to others. Sometimes I like to give my own perspective on it. A Retr",
   "content_zh": "愿主与你同在,今天祝福你,我的朋友们. 销售与交易今日的Kindle交易包括几个圣诞奉献,一个是格雷格·克克(Greg Koukl)经典,以及赛斯·刘易斯的\"梦想之小\"等. 如果有兴趣,Audible继续提供大量服务——3个月服务,再加上0.99美元的20美元奖金。 随时可以取消订阅.\n\n推荐阅读无电话教会宣言. 这篇文章对于在教堂使用我们的电话的后果,提供了很多思考的机会. “崇拜中的分裂将永远与我们同在,但这并不意味着我们应当走进高速公路和树篱并尽可能多地分散注意力。\n\n在这里,我们应当注意到,教会中有一些良好的分心——我想到那些婴儿哭出大惊小怪并嘲笑所有错误的时刻。 良好分心提醒我们,教会不仅仅是我们与上帝的\"单独时间\"。 我们是家庭的一部分。” 约翰·马克·科默尔的\"安静时间\"中的\"失踪的碎片\".\n\n我认为马修·宾汉姆对约翰·马克·科梅尔(John Mark Comer)书的评论, 无论是赞美还是批评, 都令人振奋。 “尽管科默确定自己是一位新教徒,但他依靠许多来自`沙漠之父和母亲'、中世纪神秘论以及现代罗马天主教和东方东正教神学家的引文来证明他对精神的食堂方法是合理的。\n\n和他之前的作品一样,他与改革派的少数继承人交往. 但对于他来说, 这并非孤立无援。 这本书与这种非抗议性的神秘传统一致,除了《圣经》中上帝所启示的文字外,大力强调主观的、与上帝的直接沟通。 一年免费小鸡\n\n你知道中西部神学院是斯普琴学院的所在地吗? 斯普琴学院是一所为王国培养学生的本科学校。 今年十一月, 头到这里进入赢 并发现其他机会 在基督这个月更深了! (赞助)罗马的拉动和恩典的承诺.\n\n克里斯·卡斯塔多(Chris Castaldo)写道那些被引向罗马的人. “你们小团体的一名成员承认, 接下来,你听到一个执事 大声问我们是否真的需要 与罗马决裂。 她已经皈依了罗马天主教。\n\n这种对话似乎在新教圈子里更加频繁地发生。 为什么?” Costi Hinn概述了对精神战争的四个相当普遍的错误认识。 “有一份基督教信仰的简短清单,其神秘之处与精神战一样多。\n\n虽然《圣经》中有些关于恶魔和恶魔活动的内容是十分清楚的,但是在幽灵世界中却有一种超自然的元素,即使最受过教育的神学学生也是谦卑的!\n\n同时,看来许多人根据自己的经历有各种观点,这不一定是负面的东西,但会导致许多误解\". 向纳尼亚走去 我个人一直喜欢阅读关于纳尼亚电影的不断增长的信息,\n\n我认为Nicholas McDonald的文章是目前为止最好的一篇文章。 他解释了自己成功改编电影的公式(Faithinity to the Electric + Thought Innoversations = Great Film Refect),并说明了他是否觉得自己对魔术师的侄女有希望。 4个惩罚 当你觉得有罪 为你付出。\n\n我认为大多数人对不时的奉献感到内疚. 当你这样做的时候,你可以用一些方法纠正你的思想和行动方式。 我要求这个网站的读者告诉我他们喜欢什么, 有时候,我喜欢自己来看待它。 调试器",
   "image": "https://www.challies.com/media/2026/05/Thursday-1.jpg",
   "author": "Tim Challies",
