  {
   "title": "Salvation Makes You Part of a Family: The Corporate Component of Conversion",
   "url": "https://www.9marks.org/article/salvation-makes-you-part-of-a-family-the-corporate-component-of-conversion/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=salvation-makes-you-part-of-a-family-the-corporate-component-of-conversion",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "9Marks",
   "source_url": "https://9marks.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "Our corporate unity in Christ is not just an implication of conversion; it’s part of the very thing. Being reconciled to God’s people is distinct from but inseparable from being reconciled to God.   The post  Salvation Makes You Part of a Family: The Corporate Component of Conversion  appeared first on  9Marks .",
   "summary_zh": "我们在基督里的公司合一不仅仅是皈依的含义；它也是事情的一部分。与神的子民和好有别于与神和好，但不可分割。后救赎使你成为家庭的一部分：皈依的企业组成部分首先出现在9Marks上。",
   "title_zh": "救赎使你成为家庭的一部分：皈依的企业组成部分",
   "content": "Abstract : Jonathan Leeman highlights the corporate component of conversion, pointing out that God not only reconciles us to himself through Christ but also to one another. While our (vertical) reconciliation to God is foundational and primary, our (horizontal) reconciliation to others is necessarily bound up with our salvation. Conversion makes us part of God’s people, and this corporate aspect of our salvation should compel us to join a local church. Editor’s Note: This article is taken from Church Matters, the 9Marks journal for pastors, in the issue titled Conversion . If your doctrine of conversion is missing the corporate element, it’s missing something essential. Jesus died for a people (see Mark 10:45). He saves us as individuals, and he saves us into a people. Salvation includes a family. If you’re not convinced, jump straight to these parallel statements from Peter: Once you were not a people, but now you are God’s people; once you had not received mercy, but now you have received mercy. (1 Pet. 2:10) If someone asks you how you became a Christian, you probably emphasize the second line in your testimony. You say something like, “I was living in sin apart from God. A friend shared the gospel with me. I recognized who God is and what Christ did in dying and rising again. Therefore, I repented and believed. Praise God, he forgave me and I received his mercy!” What a wonderful testimony. Don’t stop saying that! Widen Your Perspective But notice that Peter widens the aperture of the camera and tells us a little more about what happened in that same moment. In addition to moving from not mercy to mercy, we simultaneously moved from not a people to a people. That means our testimonies could include a little bit more. Like this: “I was living in sin apart from God, and I wanted nothing to do with God’s family, the church. A friend shared the gospel with me. I recognized who God is and what Christ did in dying and rising again. Therefore, I repented and believed. Praise God, he forgave me and I received his mercy! I also realized that—wow!—I was part of a family now, the church.” Do you see what I mean by the “corporate” component of conversion? We’re saved into the universal church. That’s not to say we should put the corporate element out front. One might think of N. T. Wright’s well-known line about justification being “not so much about soteriology as about ecclesiology; not so much about salvation as about the church . ” N.T. Wright, What Saint Paul Really Said (Eerdmans, 20 1 4), 1 1 9. This is a clear example, in Douglas Moo’s almost-as-well-known line, of backgrounding what the New Testament foregrounds, and foregrounding what the New Testament backgrounds (as cited in D. A. Carson, “Faith and Faithfulness,” Ligonier, February 1 , 20 1 0, https://learn.ligonier.org/articles/faith-and-faithfulness). There can be no true reconciliation between humans until individual sinners are first reconciled to God. The horizontal necessarily follows the vertical. Ecclesiology necessarily follows soteriology. Which is to say, the corporate element must not come first, lest we lose salvation altogether. Vertical and Horizontal But it must come. Indeed, the corporate component must remain within the structure of the doctrine of conversion itself. Our corporate unity in Christ is not just an implication of conversion; it’s part of the very thing. Being reconciled to God’s people is distinct from but inseparable from being reconciled to God. These two elements of conversion are wonderfully put on display in Ephesians 2 with two instances of the word “but.” The first comes as Paul narrates man’s rescue from sin and death (vv. 1–10), which hinges on the words “ But God, being rich in mercy . . . ” (v. 4). Those words introduce God’s saving love and the fact that he has “raised us up with [Christ] and seated us with him in the heavenly places in Christ Jesus” (v. 6). There is your vertical reconciliation. We’ve been raised up. Yet there’s",
   "content_zh": "摘要:乔纳森·李曼(Jonathan Leeman)强调转会中的公司成分,指出上帝不仅通过基督来调和我们自己,而且相互调和. 虽然我们与上帝的(纵向)和解是基础和首要的,但我们与他人的(横向)和解必然与我们的拯救联系在一起。\n\n皈依让我们成为上帝人民的一部分,我们拯救的这一整体方面应该迫使我们加入当地的教会。 编辑说明:这篇文章取自9Marks牧师杂志《教会事务》, 如果你的转换理论 缺少公司要素, 它缺少一些重要的东西。 耶稣为一民族而死(见马克10:45).\n\n他拯救我们作为个人,把我们救入一个民族. 救世主包括一个家庭。 若你不相信, 以前,你们不是民众,而现在你们是真主的民众;以前,你们没有蒙主的怜悯,现在你们却蒙主的怜悯。 (原始内容存档于2018-09-29) (中文(简体) ).\n\n2:10 如果有人问你如何成为基督徒,你可能强调你证词中的第二行. 你说:我确是在罪中,与真主无关。 一个朋友跟我分享福音 我认出了上帝是谁 以及基督在死后和复活中做了什么 因此,我忏悔并相信。 赞美上帝,他原谅我,我得到了他的怜悯!” 多么美妙的证词。\n\n不要停止说! 拓宽视角 但请注意,彼得拓宽了相机的孔径,告诉我们更多关于同一时刻发生的事情. 除了从不怜悯到怜悯之外,我们还同时从一个民族转变为一个民族。 这意味着我们的证词可以包括更多一点。\n\n像这样:\"我活在罪中,除了上帝之外,我不希望与上帝的家人,即教会有任何关系. 一个朋友跟我分享福音 我认出了上帝是谁 以及基督在死后和复活中做了什么 因此,我忏悔并相信。 赞美上帝,他原谅我 我得到了他的怜悯!\n\n我也意识到,——哇!——我现在是一个家庭的一部分,即教会。” 你懂我的意思吗? 我们被救进世界教会。 这不是说我们应该把公司因素放在首位。 人们或许会想到N. T. Wright关于理由的一句众所周知的话: \" 与其说是理论,不如说是理论;\n\nN. T. Wright, What Saint Paul Really Said (Eerdmans, 20 1 4), 1 119。 这在道格拉斯·穆(Douglas Moo)几乎广为人知的一行中是一个明显的例子,说明新约的前身是什么,以及新约前身是什么(如D.\n\n卡森,“信仰与信仰”,利戈尼埃,2010年2月1日,https://learn.ligonier.org/articles/feature- and-feative. 在个别罪人首先与上帝和解之前,人类之间不可能有真正的和解. 水平必须跟随垂直。 遗传学必然跟随神经学.\n\n也就是说,公司要素不能先来,以免我们完全失去救赎。 垂直和水平 但它必须来。 实际上,公司组成部分必须保留在转换理论本身的结构之内。 我们企业在基督中的团结并不仅仅是皈依的含意,而是其中的一部分。\n\n与真主的宗族和解,与真主和解是分不开的。 在以弗所2中,将这两个转换要素用“但”一词的两起例子作了精彩的展示。 第一种说法是保罗讲述了人类从罪孽和死亡中解救出来(vv. 1-10),这取决于 \" 但上帝,充满了慈悲. \" (v.\n\n这些话介绍了上帝的救世主之爱,以及他 \" 使我们与[基督]一起在基督耶稣的天上同坐 \" (v.6)的事实。 这就是你的垂直调和。 我们长大了。 然而,还有",
   "image": "https://www.9marks.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/The-Corporate-Component-of-Conversion--scaled.jpg",
   "author": "Jeri Choi",
   "tags": [],
   "language": "en",
   "country": "US",
   "region": "",
   "stance": "evangelical",
   "flags": [],
   "priority": 2,
   "fetched_at": "2026-11-11T00:25:57.151746",
   "extra": {
    "feed_type": "rss20"
   },
   "id": "b1e1b4bdeaae99cc"
  },
  {
   "title": "Partners in Christ",
   "url": "https://odb.org/2026/11/06/",
   "category": "devotional",
