   "source_url": "https://theaquilareport.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-06",
   "summary": "Liturgical worship remains the most clearly reflective of God’s holiness, love, beauty, and mystery that we have from the Christian era. The work of Calvin and his followers in the Reformation and later can perhaps best be understood as a needed corrective to the ritualistic worship of the late medieval period, which focused on ceremony...  Continue Reading",
   "summary_zh": "礼仪崇拜仍然是我们从基督教时代开始，最清楚地反映出神的圣洁、爱、美丽和奥秘。加尔文和他的追随者在宗教改革和后来的工作，也许最好被理解为对中世纪晚期仪式崇拜的必要纠正，这种崇拜侧重于仪式……继续阅读",
   "title_zh": "改革宗崇拜及其理由--第2部分",
   "content": "Liturgical worship remains the most clearly reflective of God’s holiness, love, beauty, and mystery that we have from the Christian era. The work of Calvin and his followers in the Reformation and later can perhaps best be understood as a needed corrective to the ritualistic worship of the late medieval period, which focused on ceremony... Continue Reading",
   "content_zh": "礼仪崇拜仍然是我们从基督教时代开始，最清楚地反映出神的圣洁、爱、美丽和奥秘。加尔文和他的追随者在宗教改革和后来的工作，也许最好被理解为对中世纪晚期仪式崇拜的必要纠正，这种崇拜侧重于仪式……继续阅读",
