   "published": "2026-11-07",
   "summary": "This passage makes an important point—afflictions (or trials, depending on the translation) have a purpose. The purpose is encouragement. 2 Corinthians 1:1–7 (ESV) Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, To the church of God that is at Corinth, with all the saints who are...  Continue Reading",
   "summary_zh": "这段经文提出了一个重要的观点--苦难（或考验，取决于翻译）是有目的的。目的是鼓励。哥林多后书1: 1–7 （ ESV ）保罗，基督耶稣的使徒，奉神的旨意，和我们的兄弟提摩太，致哥林多神的教会，与所有的圣徒……继续阅读",
   "title_zh": "舒适",
   "content": "This passage makes an important point—afflictions (or trials, depending on the translation) have a purpose. The purpose is encouragement.     2 Corinthians 1:1–7 (ESV) Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, To the church of God that is at Corinth, with all the saints who are... Continue Reading",
   "content_zh": "这段经文提出了一个重要的观点--苦难（或考验，取决于翻译）是有目的的。目的是鼓励。哥林多后书1: 1–7 （ ESV ）保罗，基督耶稣的使徒，奉神的旨意，和我们的兄弟提摩太，致哥林多神的教会，与所有的圣徒……继续阅读",
