  {
   "title": "Time and Struggles",
   "url": "https://odb.org/2026/11/09/",
   "category": "devotional",
   "source": "Our Daily Bread (English)",
   "source_url": "https://odb.org/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "Josephine Cochrane (1839-1913) was tired of having her dishes damaged by handwashing, so she decided to create a dishwasher. Shortly after she began her design, her husband passed away, leaving her in debt. Those circumstances reinforced her need to succeed.",
   "summary_zh": "Josephine Cochrane （ 1839-1913 ）厌倦了洗手损坏她的碗碟，所以她决定制作一台洗碗机。在她开始设计后不久，她的丈夫去世了，让她负债累累。这些情况强化了她成功的需要。",
   "title_zh": "时间和挣扎",
   "content": "Josephine Cochrane (1839-1913) was tired of having her dishes damaged by handwashing, so she decided to create a dishwasher. Shortly after she began her design, her husband passed away, leaving her in debt. Those circumstances reinforced her need to succeed.",
   "content_zh": "Josephine Cochrane （ 1839-1913 ）厌倦了洗手损坏她的碗碟，所以她决定制作一台洗碗机。在她开始设计后不久，她的丈夫去世了，让她负债累累。这些情况强化了她成功的需要。",
   "image": "https://odb.org/globalassets/global/logos/parent-logos/odb_parentbrand_logo_8-9-24_fullclr_icon.png?width=1200&height=680&rmode=max",
