   "summary": "Christians don’t shy away from the horror of human suffering, perhaps because the central symbol of our faith is a tortured man on a cross gasping for air. And to the question posed by Night, in that scene with the boy being hanged—“Where is God?!”—the Christian answer transposes the words of Wiesel—“He is here”—into a...  Continue Reading",
