   "source_url": "https://www.christianitytoday.com/feed/",
   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "The worship wars have left us feeling weary and worn out. It sounds like Jesus is my boyfriend. There is too much I and not enough Thou. God isn’t the subject of all the verbs. We’ve all heard variations of these tired complaints about contemporary worship music by traditionalists (of which I am one). And  Read more...   The post  Why Your Favorite Worship Song’s Grammar Matters  appeared first on  Christianity Today .",
   "summary_zh": "崇拜战争让我们感到疲惫和疲惫。听起来耶稣是我的男朋友。我太多，你太少。神不是所有动词的主语。我们都听说过传统主义者（我是其中之一）对当代崇拜音乐的疲惫不堪的抱怨。阅读更多……《为什么你最喜欢的崇拜歌曲的语法很重要》一文首次出现在《今日基督教》上。",
   "title_zh": "为什么你最喜欢的崇拜歌曲的语法很重要",
   "content": "The worship wars have left us feeling weary and worn out. It sounds like Jesus is my boyfriend. There is too much I and not enough Thou. God isn’t the subject of all the verbs. We’ve all heard variations of these tired complaints about contemporary worship music by traditionalists (of which I am one). And Read more... The post Why Your Favorite Worship Song’s Grammar Matters appeared first on Christianity Today .",
