   "summary": "Christianity demands obedience, but the creed of self-creation demands something far more merciless: total self-generation. Having rejected the yoke of Christ, the soul is told to become its own cosmic anchor, its own moral authority, and the sole author of its existential purpose. What began as a desperate bid for freedom becomes the impossible burden...  Continue Reading",
