   "title_zh": "Grace Is Not for Sale",
   "content": "Rejecting the prosperity gospel does not mean God is against our wellbeing. The Bible does not teach a poverty gospel either. God cares about daily bread, honours hard work, and provides for His children (Matthew 6:31–33). But grace gives far more than money can. In Christ we have been blessed “with every spiritual blessing” (Ephesians... Continue Reading",
   "content_zh": "拒绝成功福音并不意味着神违背了我们的福祉。圣经也没有教导贫穷福音。神关心每日的食物，尊重辛勤工作，并供应祂的儿女（马太福音6:31 –33 ）。但恩典给予的远远超过金钱所能给予的。在基督里，我们“蒙受属灵的祝福” （以弗所书……继续阅读",
