   "published": "2026-11-11",
   "summary": "Tuesday is the day most publishers release their new books. Here is a look at the Christian books that came our way this week, including Biblical and Theological Studies, From Silence to Sinai. See Also New and Notable Christian Books for October 2026 (Plus a Preview of November) This Week in Christian Books (October 27, 2026) Best Commentaries on Leviticus",
   "summary_zh": "周二是大多数出版商发布新书的日子。以下是本周出现的基督教书籍，包括圣经和神学研究，从沉默到西奈。另请参阅2026年10月新的和著名的基督教书籍（加上11月的预览）本周基督教书籍（ 2026年10月27日）对利未记的最佳评论",
   "title_zh": "本周基督教书籍（ 2026年11月10日）",
   "content": "Tuesday is the day most publishers release their new books, so each week I like to let you know what has just come our way from the publishers I follow most closely. It is a quieter week than the last one, but it brings a revised edition of B. B. Warfield’s Biblical and Theological Studies, Alex Duke’s guided tour of Exodus (for which I provided a foreword), and two Crossway editions marking 500 years since William Tyndale’s English New Testament. On the academic side, you’ll find several noteworthy titles, including the New International Commentary on the Old Testament volume on Daniel 7–12. In each case, I’ve included the publisher’s description. Books for Everyone Zondervan From Silence to Sinai A Guided Tour of Exodus Alex Duke Publisher’s description What adjectives would you use to describe the Bible? Inspired. Amazing. Unique. Authoritative. Perfect. Pure. Life-changing. Those descriptions are all deserved. Your pastors and parents and Sunday School teachers were right. There’s no book like God’s Book. Here’s another adjective: confusing. The Bible can be confusing, especially certain parts of the Old Testament. Moments after coming across something inspiring and encouraging, you’ll read something that makes you wonder, What is even happening right now!? The book of Exodus is no exception. This sequel to Genesis begins with God’s surprising silence. What a stark contrast to Genesis, where God’s words set everything in motion. It then tells the story of God’s miraculous liberation of his people, complete with frogs falling from the sky and life-saving blood being painted over doorways. Finally, for the last half of the book, the action slows down as the people of God gather at the mountain of God to receive the Law of God in order to engage in the worship of God. From silence to Sinai, that’s the story of Exodus. To understand it all, most of us will need a guide. We’ll need some help. That’s what From Silence to Sinai is for. Alex Duke walks readers through the book of Exodus to show that nothing in God’s story is wasted—not the silence, not the ten signs, and not even the confusing parts. In Exodus, God is not absent, random, or unclear. He is revealing himself, redeeming his people, and teaching them how to live in his presence. Buy it at Amazon or Westminster Books . B&H The First Five Beating the Odds and Thriving as a Ministry Leader Kyle Worley and Joseph Worley Publisher’s description Is it possible to do more than survive in ministry leadership? Could you actually thrive? The alarming reality is that most ministry leaders will not make it more than five years in leadership. Burnout, lack of training, and an absence of coaches are all pitfalls on the road to sustainable ministry leadership. But there is a different roadmap for those willing to learn. In The First Five , Joseph and Kyle Worley present a pathway for thriving in ministry leadership. With over sixty years of experience, across churches of every size and shape, they provide a biblically rooted and tested approach to the personal, professional, and pastoral dynamics of ministry leadership. The First Five is designed to be a manual for new ministry leaders and those leading them. Don’t just read this book—use it! You can do more than survive as a ministry leader. We believe you can thrive. Buy it at Amazon . Preorder · releases Wednesday, November 11 P&R Biblical and Theological Studies Revised and Enhanced Benjamin B. Warfield, edited by John J. Hughes Endorsed by: Vern S. Poythress, Thomas R. Schreiner, R. Scott Clark, Donald Macleod, and Richard C. Gamble Publisher’s description Classic articles from Warfield, enhanced for ease of reading, explore God, predestination, the supernaturalism of Christianity, the antiquity and unity of the human race, mysticism, and the prophecies of Paul. The Classic Warfield Collection presents scholars, students, and educated laypeople with reedited, unabridged versions of B. B. Warfield’s most luminous articles, enhan",
   "content_zh": "星期二是大多数出版商发布新书的一天, 所以我每个星期都想告诉你, 我最密切地关注的出版商 给我们带来了什么。 这周比上一周更安静,但带来了B. B.\n\n沃菲尔德的圣经和神学研究,亚历克斯·杜克对Exodus的导游(我为此提供了前言),以及两个十字路口版,标志着威廉·廷达勒的\"英语新约\"(English New Tondament)以来的500年. 在学术方面,你会发现几个值得注意的标题,包括丹尼尔7-12上的旧约卷的新国际评注。\n\n每一次,我都包括出版商的描述。 从沉默到西奈的图书, 你用什么形容词来形容圣经? 发菩提心. 厉害 独一无二 专权性. 不错 纯净. 改变生活。 这些描述都是值得的。 你的牧师和家长 以及星期日学校的老师是对的\n\n没有像上帝的书那样的书。 以下是另一个形容词:令人困惑。 圣经可以令人困惑,特别是旧约中的某些部分. 在经历了一些鼓舞人心和鼓舞人心的事情之后, 你会读到一些让你感到奇怪的东西, 出家经卷亦无例外. 创世纪的续集开始于上帝令人惊讶的沉默。\n\n与创世纪的鲜明对比,上帝的言语让一切动起来. 它讲述了上帝奇迹般地解放其人民的故事,最后是青蛙从天而降,在门道上画出拯救生命的鲜血。\n\n最后,在书的后半段,随着上帝的百姓聚集在神的山上接受神的律法,以从事对神的崇拜,这一行动放缓了. 从沉默到西奈,这就是出埃及的故事。 为了了解这一切,我们大多数人都需要一个指南。 需要帮助。 从沉默到西奈,\n\n亚历克斯·杜克(Alex Duke)通过《出神记》的书向读者表明,上帝的故事中没有任何东西是浪费的,不是沉默,不是十种迹象,甚至连令人困惑的部分也没有。 在出埃及语中,上帝不是缺席,是随意的,或者是不明确的. 他正在揭露自己,救赎他的人民,并教他们如何在他面前生活。 在亚马逊或威斯敏斯特书店买的\n\nB&H 前5名击败奇数 并担任部领导 Kyle Worley 和 Joseph Worley 出版社的描述 在部委领导层中能否做更多的工作? 你真的能兴旺起来吗? 令人震惊的现实是,大多数部委领导人担任领导不超过五年。\n\n燃烧、缺乏培训以及缺乏教练都是实现可持续部委领导道路上的陷阱。 但对于愿意学习的人,有不同的路线图。 在前五卷中,约瑟夫和凯尔·沃利提出了在部领导中蓬勃发展的途径。\n\n具有60多年的经验,各种大小和形状的教会都对部委领导的个人、专业和牧业动态提供了具有圣经根源和考验的方法。 \" 前五 \" 旨在为新的部委领导人和领导者编写手册。 不要只读这本书, 作为部会领导,你可以做的不只是生存。\n\n我们相信你能够蓬勃发展 买在亚马逊。 Preorder ^ 11月11日,星期三发布 P&R Biblical and Theological Studies Review and University Benjamin B. Warfield,由约翰·休斯(英语:John J. Hughes)编辑,弗恩·S·波伊雷斯(英语:Vern S. Poythress),托马斯·R·施雷纳(英语:Thomas R. Schreiner),R·斯科特·克拉克,唐纳德·麦克勒德(英语:Donald Macleod)和理查德·C.\n\nGamble Publishers的描述来自沃菲尔德的经典文章,为方便阅读而强化,探索上帝,宿命,基督教的超自然主义,人类的古老和团结,神秘主义,保罗的预言. \"古典战地集\"向学者,学生,以及受过教育的非专业人士介绍了编年史,未删节的B. B.\n\n沃菲尔德最发光的文章,恩汉",
